    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63691&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Museum Custodian (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Museum Custodian (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63691 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities This role serves as a member of the General Museum Housekeeping Team, performing custodial tasks such as floor maintenance, public restrooms cleaning and stocking, mopping, dusting, etc. Cleans and sanitizes all public spaces and restrooms throughout the Sarasota Campus Complex during the day. Restocks tissue, towels, and hand soap supplies. Completes assigned daily tasks in campus venue to include prepare the campus to open, cleaning glass, dusting, sweeping, mopping, and emptying wastebaskets. Respond to service calls. Clean special event areas as needed: clearing refuse and using appropriate tools to remove stains and scrub hard surfaces. Complete assigned work orders and stock custodial closets according to supply request sheets or as needed. Drives custodial golf carts to traverse the 66 acre campus to deliver supplies and carry equipment. Clear trash from Sarasota Campus Complex grounds and clean exterior surfaces. Empty and transport recycling. Performs custodial maintenance projects. Completes other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations and provides general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum, which may include supporting events and general assistance as needed. Qualifications Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire Due to the need to drive golf carts in this role, applicants must be 18 years of age or older. 9th-grade education or higher Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position, to include moving objects up to 45lbs, working with chemicals, climbing and descending stairs, standing and walking for extended periods. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to maintaining high standards of cleanliness and organization. Ability to: Communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Work independently while contributing positively to a team environment. Recognize workplace safety hazards and implement appropriate safety precautions. Knowledge of the safe operation of custodial equipment, machinery, tools, and cleaning materials. Problem-solving skills with the ability to identify issues and take appropriate corrective action. Verbal fluency in additional language(s) besides English. Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2773. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $33,408 or higher annually. Final offer amount will be determined based on the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. This position is based in Sarasota, FL. Employees are required to wear the standard issue uniform while at work. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. This posting is to fill multiple roles. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours Friday to Tuesday from 10:00 AM to 6:30 PM with a half hour meal period. Weekends, weekdays, evenings, and holidays may be required per the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63587&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Export Control Officer",
      "description": "Export Control Officer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63587 Location Remote Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Research, Integrity, Security & Ethics within the Division of Research seeks to fill the role of Export Control Officer. Responsibilities This role will develop, implement, and maintain the university's export control compliance program. Interpret and apply federal regulations including ITAR, EAR, OFAC, and related research security requirements. Develop policies, procedures, guidance documents, and internal controls to ensure institutional compliance and minimize regulatory risk. Monitor regulatory and agency changes and recommend program modifications as necessary. Review research proposals, contracts, grants, agreements, disclosures, international collaborations, shipments, and activities for export control implications. Evaluate foreign national participation, controlled technologies, technical data, and restricted research requirements. Provide recommendations and compliance determinations to faculty, staff, and leadership. Will develop, implement, and monitor Technology Control Plans (TCPs) and related security measures for export-controlled research and controlled unclassified information. Conduct risk assessments, compliance reviews, and monitoring activities to ensure adherence to institutional and regulatory requirements. Oversee restricted party screening and international compliance review processes. Evaluate international visitors, collaborators, vendors, sponsors, and research partners for sanctions or export control concerns. Document determinations and maintain required records. Develop and deliver training, educational programs, and compliance resources related to export controls, research security, international collaborations, foreign influence, and related regulatory requirements. Promote awareness and compliance across the research community. Prepare license applications and regulatory submissions when required. Serve as the university liaison with federal regulatory agencies. Investigate potential compliance concerns, recommend corrective actions, maintain required records, and prepare reports for institutional leadership. Qualifications Bachelor's degree with six years of professional experience. Four years of experience will need to be in research compliance, export controls, regulatory compliance, research administration, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Our Ideal candidate would have experience within a higher education setting, developing and implementing compliance programs and plans, and hold current certifications of ITAR, EAR, and OFAC. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position has been designated as eligible for remote work based on the current position/job functions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63819&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Producer/Reporter - The Florida Channel",
      "description": "Producer/Reporter - The Florida Channel Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63819 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Florida Channel Responsibilities Serves as Producer for Capitol Update/News Brief. Duties include but are not limited to: Assisting in researching and assigning stories, overseeing rundowns, and reviewing information for content and accuracy. Coordinates with other departments in the timely delivery of TFC programs. Demonstrates good organization and communication skills to carry out assignments with limited supervision. Able to think creatively and work in a team environment. Able to make independent, sound news decisions during live productions to include, exclude or modify information presented. Ability to accurately time shows and respond quickly to issues that may arise in live production. Ability to monitor daily progress of each team member to keep production on deadline and offer assistance as needed. Works with Executive Director, News Manager and Producers (as needed) to establish and implement best practices related to Rundown Approval Process and Script Approval Guidelines to ensure agreement on format, content, structure and flow of programming. Serves as a Reporter for Capitol Update/News Brief, Producer/Reporter for Florida Crossroads and other TFC Programming. Duties include but are not limited to: Being proactive in originating, researching, developing, and following through with ideas; writing clear and concise scripts on deadline; interviewing individuals (for on-air or background use) in a professional, independent manner; performing live shots, set shots, and standups; compiling information for graphics or other visual elements used to creatively and effectively complete a program or program segment. Ability to utilize social media and other news gathering techniques to focus on initial development and ongoing contact with lawmakers, staff, policymakers, and other key sources critical to newsgathering. Required to follow established guidelines and policy while striving to maintain TFC’s integrity and reputation. Adheres to related timelines to ensure all standards, needs and deadlines are met. Provides production support. Travel is required and ability to work a flexible schedule, as needed. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Strong writing and research skills. Experience writing scripts on deadline. The ability to think creatively and carry out specific program concepts after receiving general guidance – but with limited supervision. On-camera experience in a professional newsroom environment. Attention to detail; effective time management and organizational skills. The ability to work as part of a team on tight deadlines. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to deal with fast-changing situations are necessary, often in public. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position includes travel and a schedule that may include weekends and/or evenings. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63825&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Regional Program Manager, Miami Dade Recruitment",
      "description": "Regional Program Manager, Miami Dade Recruitment Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63825 Location Remote Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Admissions Responsibilities The Office of Admissions is a unit within the Division of Enrollment Management, which is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions, Office of the University Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management’s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the student's development and progression in their academic experience – from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families and to campus partners across the University. Manages the development, coordination, and implementation of regional recruitment programs and strategic partnership initiatives, with primary responsibility for advancing FSU’s relationship with Miami Dade College. Establishes and maintains strong relationships with Miami Dade College (MDC) to increase the University’s visibility and translating FSU/MDC articulation agreement to create transparent pathways and enhanced advising for MDC students to transfer to the university. Collaborates with campus partners, including academic colleges, student services, and other University offices, to coordinate regional recruitment initiatives and support student enrollment. Evaluates recruitment activity and enrollment trends within the Miami-Dade market and uses available data to identify opportunities, challenges, and strategies for increasing FSU's market penetration. Establishes and sustains a broad network of educational and community partners that support long-term recruitment efforts, increase institutional visibility, and promote continued enrollment growth throughout the region. Plans, manages, and evaluates comprehensive regional recruitment and student engagement initiatives for first-year and transfer populations throughout Miami-Dade county and other areas of South Florida. Develops and implements strategic recruitment plans with measurable objectives related to prospective student engagement, application generation, admission, enrollment, and yield. Coordinates outreach activities and other targeted recruitment initiatives. Establishes and maintains productive relationships with educational stakeholders to expand access to FSU and strengthen the university’s recruitment pipeline. Provides guidance regarding undergraduate admissions requirements, university policies, application procedures, and transfer pathways to prospective students and educational partners. Assesses the effectiveness of recruitment activities, identifies opportunities to improve outreach and engagement, and adjusts strategies based on regional enrollment trends, student interests, and institutional priorities. Coordinates regional recruitment activities with internal and external stakeholders to ensure consistent messaging, effective resource utilization, and alignment with university enrollment objectives. The position requires operation of a motor vehicle to perform assigned responsibilities. Participates in the evaluation of first-year and transfer applications for admission to the University. Applies university admissions standards, policies, and procedures to support consistent and accurate application review and decision-making. Responsible for the implementation of university policies and procedures as they relate to Undergraduate Admissions. Collaborates with appropriate admissions personnel to address application-related questions, resolve procedural issues, and support the effective administration of undergraduate admissions. Contributes to the development, review, and evaluation of policies, procedures, and operational practices that support regional recruitment and undergraduate admissions. Analyzes program activities, recruitment outcomes, and operational processes to identify opportunities for improvement and recommends strategies to senior leadership to enhance program effectiveness and support enrollment goals. Participates in establishing program objectives, performance measures, implementation strategies, and operational priorities for the Office of Admissions. Collaborates with Admissions leadership and university stakeholders to support the development and implementation of recruitment initiatives, policies, procedures, and staffing strategies. Evaluates emerging recruitment needs and recommends adjustments to program activities to strengthen service delivery, operational efficiency, and student engagement. Provides cross-functional support to other Admissions sections during peak operational periods and assists with special projects and university initiatives as needed to advance the goals of the Office of Admissions. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications A bachelor’s degree in a relevant field and at least two years of related experience. A strong understanding of the value and benefits of a comprehensive education. Excellent public speaking skills are essential, along with proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, or comparable software. Ideal candidates are energetic, detail-oriented, and able to work effectively both independently and collaboratively. Candidates should demonstrate strong organizational, analytical, and time-management skills, with the ability to prioritize competing responsibilities, manage multiple assignments simultaneously, and consistently meet deadlines. Preference will be given to candidates who are Florida State University graduates and fluent in Spanish. Experience working in higher education admissions, reviewing academic transcripts, and interpreting and applying admissions test results is desirable. Candidates should demonstrate strong analytical and organizational skills, including the ability to review, interpret, and organize data and information, as well as follow through on assigned tasks. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both verbal and written, are essential for establishing and maintaining effective working relationships with colleagues and stakeholders in a virtual setting. Successful candidates will demonstrate initiative, sound judgment, problem-solving abilities, and accountability for completing assignments with minimal supervision. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Mid $50,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position has been designated as eligible for remote work based on the current position/job functions. Applicants must be able to maintain a home-based office within the designated service area. This position requires the flexibility to work evenings and weekends. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63830&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Temporary Exam Proctors - Fall 2026 (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Temporary Exam Proctors - Fall 2026 (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63830 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities The Florida State University College of Law is seeking reliable, professional, and detail-oriented individuals to serve as Exam Proctors during the Fall 2026 examination period. Proctors assist with the administration of law school examinations, including exams administered to students with approved testing accommodations. Proctor law school examinations in accordance with established procedures and exam policies. Monitor standard and accommodated testing environments to ensure exam integrity and compliance with testing rules. Track testing times, including approved extended-time accommodations and authorized breaks. Distribute, collect, and secure examination materials. Verify student attendance and maintain accurate testing records. Report any testing irregularities or concerns to law school staff. Maintain confidentiality regarding student records, accommodations, and exam content. Interact professionally with students, faculty, and staff. Qualifications Bachelor's degree. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow instructions and procedures. Dependable, punctual, and professional. Ability to remain attentive during extended testing periods. Strong communication and organizational skills. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion Preferred Qualifications Prior proctoring, educational, administrative, or student-support experience is preferred but not required. Contact Info If you have any questions, please contact the College of Law's HR Team University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Schedule: Work assignments will vary based on the examination schedule and student accommodation needs. Exam assignments occur during the law school's final examination period from November 30 through December 11, 2026. The schedules listed below reflects an estimated coverage window in which proctors are needed. Exam Proctor Shifts: Morning : 8am-12:30pm Morning Extended: 8am-3pm Afternoon: 1pm-5:30pm Afternoon Extended: 1pm-7pm Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63730&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Academic & Student Services",
      "description": "Program Manager, Academic & Student Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63730 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Housing Responsibilities STUDENT GROUP ADVISING: Serve as the advisor for student leadership groups, including the Inter-Residence Hall Council (IRHC) and National Residence Hall Honorary (NRHH) chapter; plan and implement training for executive board members and hall councils; coordinate travel arrangements and serve as the delegation advisor for student group conferences; provide oversight of fiscal management of various funds related to IRHC and NRHH; work closely with Student Government Association (SGA) to ensure compliance with policies, procedures, and advisor training. STUDENT PROGRAMMING: work with staff and students to develop and implement large scale programs in accordance with Residential Curriculum; assess annual and on-going NRHH and IRHC programs and officer training. LEADERSHIP DEVELOPMENT: Develop and conduct ongoing training and professional development for hall council advisors; coordinate and develop strategies to connect student engagement with student learning; coordinate COMPASS Leadership retreat; complete other duties as assigned in support of University Housing. CAMPUS REPRESENTATION: work with campus partners to share resources for students and staff related to leadership development; participate and represent leadership programs in campus wide traditions such as Family Weekend, Homecoming, and philanthropy. SUPERVISION: Provide daily leadership, supervision, professional development, and evaluation for a graduate assistant working in Residence Life with a focus on student leadership and programming. Qualifications Master's degree in higher education administration, student personnel, counseling or related field and one year of experience. Full-time or graduate housing/residence life experience in college/university setting required. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
