    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63659&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business)",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63659 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Finance Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Florida State University’s Herbert Wertheim College of Business seeks applications for a non-tenure track full-time teaching faculty position in Finance. The expected teaching load is four courses per semester. Specific course assignments are dependent upon the department’s needs. In addition to teaching, the candidate is expected to participate in the department, college and university service activities. The department presently has a need for industry outreach. The position is scheduled to start in Fall 2027. Qualifications Candidates for this position must have earned or be near completion of a Ph.D. in Finance or related discipline. Degree must be conferred prior to the position start date. Preferred Qualifications Candidates should demonstrate the ability to independently develop and manage courses and have a record of excellent teaching at the AACSB accredited institution. Preference will be given to the applicants with industry experience. Excellent written and communication skills in English are required. Contact Info Please contact The Recruitment Team if you have any questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Florida State University is a Carnegie-classified R1 research university located in Tallahassee, Florida, the state capital, with enrollment exceeding 46,000 students. In the 2027 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Florida State ranks No. 59 among national universities and No. 24 among public universities in the United States. The Herbert Wertheim College of Business enrolls approximately 8,500 students seeking business degrees across undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs. The Department of Finance offers programs and courses at the undergraduate, master’s, and Ph.D. levels. Graduate offerings include the Master of Science in Finance (MSF), the Ph.D. in Business Administration with a major in Finance, and MBA programs offered in full-time, evening, and online formats. Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates graduating in 2026/2027 are also required to submit transcripts. Recommendation letters can be submitted with the application or emailed to The Recruitment Team . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled or March 1, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
