    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63712&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "FSUS Classroom Substitute, 2026-2027 (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "FSUS Classroom Substitute, 2026-2027 (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63712 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities Substitutes for teachers grades K-12. Works with teachers in the classroom to help students. Supervises the classroom in teacher's absence. Completes paperwork under the teacher's direction. May include other student supervisory duties as needed. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Must be able to provide three professional references Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree with experience working in a school setting. Florida Teaching Certificate. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. Contact Info Jaye Corbett University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.25 per hour. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63063&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Animal Care",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Animal Care Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63063 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Laboratory Animal Resources within the Office of Research seeks to fill the Assistant Director of Animal Care position. Responsibilities This position is responsible for providing direction for the daily operation of the animal care and husbandry program. Provides strategic oversight for all LAR-maintained facilities. Relieves the LAR Director of a wide variety of internal duties and on-the-ground decision making. Supervises the functions and activities of LAR direct animal care staff. Ensures that animal care staff follow established operating procedures. Schedules, assigns and re-assigns work to ensure efficient utilization of manpower, equipment and facilities. Determines needs and makes recommendations for staffing and new/replacement equipment and/or services. Coordinates hiring, orienting, training, assessing, disciplinary action and termination procedures for LAR direct animal care staff. Communicate with faculty and investigators to determine project requirements for animal resources, housing, and care. Complete and coordinate complex projects and reports, which may require significant contact with other departments and outside organizations. Participates in and provides input for planning, design and commissioning of renovations and new spaces. Develops changes to operational policies for LAR animal care and husbandry programs. This position preforms rounds in animal facilities to ensure maintenance of required sanitation standards and conformance to AAALAC, USDA, Guide, IACUC and department policies and guidelines; observes and reports noticeable deficiencies. Provides detailed written inspection reports of all the animal facilities routinely to the LAR Director. Participates in department and IACUC inspections, AAALAC site visits and other regulatory visits. Ensures that equipment and facilities are maintained in operational condition. Ensures that equipment or facility issues are reported in a timely fashion and follows through to ensure the problems are resolved. Serves as departmental property manager. Responsible for information and inventory management, and coordinating supply orders while remaining within budgetary constraints. This position provides technical expertise and instruction in animal use and experimentation. Will Assist with colony health surveillance monitoring program as needed. Will serve as acting supervisor of cage wash personnel in absence of Cage Wash and Ancillary Services Supervisor. Oversees integrated pest management program. Attends regional or national meetings periodically to remain current with industry standards and to promote teamwork and growth in LAR. Participates in emergency response planning and contingency planning for animal facilities. Rotates after hours, weekend, and holiday coverage with Cage Wash and Ancillary Services Supervisor. Perform other duties as assigned related to operation of animal facilities and animal care program. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience in a related science or research services field or a Masters and two years experience in a related science or research services field. Must hold a current LATG Certification issued by AALAS. Preferred Qualifications Experience managing personnel and operations within an academic laboratory animal care program American Association for Laboratory Animal Science Certified Manager of Animal Resources (CMAR) certification Master’s degree in laboratory animal science, veterinary science, biological science, business administration, public administration, or a related field Demonstrated ability to build and maintain collaborative relationships with investigators, animal care staff, veterinary staff, and institutional partners Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated salary range for this position is $100,000 - $140,000. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Applicants must submit a cover letter outlining their qualifications, leadership experience, and leadership philosophy. The letter should include a discussion of how the applicant would balance the highest standards of animal welfare and regulatory compliance while supporting and facilitating the research and teaching missions of the University. Applicants must provide a minimum of three professional references familiar with their work performance and leadership abilities, including each reference's relationship to the applicant, email address, and telephone number. Applicants that do not submit all required materials will not be considered. This position participates in a rotation of after hours, weekend, and holiday on-call with other LAR supervisory personnel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63703&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Director for Election Law Center (Research Faculty I 12 Month Visiting)",
      "description": "Research Director for Election Law Center (Research Faculty I 12 Month Visiting) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63703 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities The Research Director of the College of Law Election Law Center will be responsible for conducting and overseeing the Center’s empirical and statistical research projects and preparing reports and articles to disseminate the results of this research to academic, governmental, and public audiences. The Director will be involved in developing methodologies for conducing the Center’s studies, obtaining the necessary data, and conducting rigorous statistical analysis. The research the Director will oversee focuses on various election administration issues and legal questions relating to the electoral process. For example, the Center seeks to compare expert witness predictions concerning the likely impact of changes to election-related rules and procedures on metrics such as voter registration or turnout to the actual results of those legal provisions (when they are allowed to take effect). This study will help determine the accuracy and reliability of various methodologies, models, data sets, and statistical techniques frequently employed in election-related litigation. Likewise, the Center seeks to update earlier studies concerning the accuracy of information contained within voter registration databases and the inclusion of ineligible registrants, particularly in light of the rise of automatic voter registration, online registration, and interstate systems facilitating the exchange of voter information among certain states. From a qualitative perspective, the Center will also examine differences among states’ laws governing provisional ballots and canvassing. Additionally, the Research Director will assist the Executive Director of the Election Law Center in cultivating and sustaining external and internal partnerships to advance the Center’s short-term and long-term goals. Qualifications A PhD in political science, mathematics, statistics, or economics is required. Applicants with PhDs in public administration, public policy, or related fields will be considered on a case-by-case basis if they have extensive training and experience with statistical analysis and empirical research. Preferred Qualifications Required Skills Background in quantitative and statistical analysis Strong research and writing skills A collaborative and solutions-focused mentality Contact Info Maureen Wagner Vinson Executive Director of Election Law Center Florida State University College of Law Mwagner3@law.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary range: $110,000-negotiable, depending upon experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63698&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Staff Attorney for Election Law Center (Instructional Specialist I 12-Month Visiting)",
      "description": "Staff Attorney for Election Law Center (Instructional Specialist I 12-Month Visiting) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63698 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities The Staff Attorney for the College of Law Election Law Center will be responsible for assisting with the Center’s legal and other research projects; engaging in legal research and drafting for amicus briefs; coding cases for databases; gathering, organizing, and summarizing primary sources for online dissemination; and preparing reports, presentations, training materials, and articles to distribute to academic, governmental, and public audiences. This research will focus on election administration, as well as constitutional and statutory issues relating to the electoral process. Specific areas of research will depend in part on litigation that may arise in federal and state court. The staff attorney will also help prepare fifty-state surveys, for example concerning the differences among states’ laws governing provisional ballots and canvassing. The staff attorney will also assist with the preparation of caselaw databases concerning various issues such as Due Process challenges to election outcomes as well as remedies under Section 2 of the Voting Rights Act. The staff attorney may also assist with the Center’s work concerning election emergencies, including gathering and reviewing the legislative history of existing laws in the field and preparation of a potential model statute. Finally, the staff attorney will also help with the Election Law Center’s ongoing project on federal and state election contests by locating, summarizing, and organizing relevant primary sources for eventual public access through an interactive website. Additionally, the Staff Attorney will assist the Executive Director of the Election Law Center in cultivating and sustaining external and internal partnerships to advance the Center’s short-term and long-term goals. Qualifications A JD is required. Applicants with an undergraduate or graduate degree in political science, history, public administration, mathematics, statistics, or economics are preferred, but not required. Preferred Qualifications Required Skills Strong research and writing skills Ability to organize and synthesize large amounts of information A collaborative and solutions-focused mentality Non-partisan dedication to generating accurate research outcomes Contact Info Maureen Wagner Vinson Executive Director of Election Law Center Florida State University College of Law Mwagner3@law.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary range $100,000-negotiable, depending upon experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63630&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist",
      "description": "FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63630 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Responsibilities Responsible for managing contract and grant (C&G) budgets and project compliance from both FSU and FAMU within assigned departments, including Industrial & Manufacturing Engineering and Material Science & Engineering. Performs specialized C&G budgetary services, accounting services, and activities related to C&G budgetary reports, long-range budget planning, allocation of funds, and monitoring of financial reports for designated C&G budgets. Serves as a liaison between the Department, College, funding agencies, Research Foundation, Sponsored Research, and other relevant organizations. Responsible for post-award financial and administrative management of assigned C&G portfolios at both FAMU and FSU. Monitors and reconciles awards monthly; tracks expenditures, encumbrances, salary commitments, subawards, and other planned costs; and maintains forward-looking projections of available balances through project end dates. Meets regularly with PIs to review financial status, burn rate, projected balances, and required actions. Processes and supports rebudgets, budget amendments, procurement, travel, FACET (effort reporting)-related C&G questions, financial reporting, records management, and project closeout. Proactively identifies projected deficits, unspent balances, expiring funds, and other financial or compliance concerns and works with PIs and appropriate University offices to resolve them. Responsible for pre-award support for assigned faculty and units. Reviews solicitations and sponsor guidelines for eligibility, budget caps, cost-sharing obligations, F&A limitations, and submission requirements, and advises PIs accordingly. Develops and analyzes complex proposal budgets, including multi-year, cost-share, and subaward budgets, and drafts corresponding budget justifications. Applies federal, state, University, and sponsor regulations in budget construction. Collects and verifies subrecipient commitment documentation. Prepares and routes proposals in RAMP system and coordinates with Sponsored Research at FSU and FAMU to meet internal and sponsor deadlines. Serves as a departmental resource for grants administration and interprets applicable University, sponsor, and regulatory requirements for faculty and staff. Monitors assigned portfolios for financial and compliance risks, communicates concerns promptly to PIs and appropriate leadership, and recommends corrective actions. Supports consistent College grants-management procedures, timelines, internal controls, and process improvements in coordination with Research Office leadership and central University offices. Improves grants administration processes through data analysis, reporting, and development of procedures and training materials. Participates in Sponsored Research training and communicates procedural changes to assigned departments. Supports grants-related special projects and other sponsored research duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three-years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to seven years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63629&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist",
      "description": "FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63629 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Responsibilities Responsible for managing contract and grant (C&G) budgets and project compliance from both FSU and FAMU within assigned college departments, including Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering and Electrical & Computer Engineering. Performs specialized C&G budgetary services, accounting services, and activities related to C&G budgetary reports, long-range budget planning, allocation of funds, and monitoring of financial reports for designated C&G budgets. Serves as a liaison between the Department, College, funding agencies, Research Foundation, Sponsored Research, and other relevant organizations. Responsible for post-award financial and administrative management of assigned C&G portfolios at both FAMU and FSU. Monitors and reconciles awards monthly; tracks expenditures, encumbrances, salary commitments, subawards, and other planned costs; and maintains forward-looking projections of available balances through project end dates. Meets regularly with (Principal Investigators) PIs to review financial status, burn rate, projected balances, and required actions. Processes and supports rebudgets, budget amendments, procurement, travel, FACET (effort reporting)-related C&G questions, financial reporting, records management, and project closeout. Proactively identifies projected deficits, unspent balances, expiring funds, and other financial or compliance concerns and works with PIs and appropriate University offices to resolve them. Responsible for pre-award support for assigned faculty and units. Reviews solicitations and sponsor guidelines for eligibility, budget caps, cost-sharing obligations, finance and administration limitations, and submission requirements, and advises PIs accordingly. Develops and analyzes complex proposal budgets, including multi-year, cost-share, and subaward budgets, and drafts corresponding budget justifications. Applies federal, state, University, and sponsor regulations in budget construction. Collects and verifies subrecipient commitment documentation. Prepares and routes proposals in RAMP system and coordinates with Sponsored Research at FSU and FAMU to meet internal and sponsor deadlines. Serves as a departmental resource for grants administration and interprets applicable University, sponsor, and regulatory requirements for faculty and staff. Monitors assigned portfolios for financial and compliance risks, communicates concerns promptly to PIs and appropriate leadership, and recommends corrective actions. Supports consistent College grants-management procedures, timelines, internal controls, and process improvements in coordination with Research Office leadership and central University offices. Improves grants administration processes through data analysis, reporting, and development of procedures and training materials. Participates in Sponsored Research training and communicates procedural changes to assigned departments. Supports grants-related special projects and other sponsored research duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three-years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to seven years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of Uniform Guidance. Knowledge of and ability to apply Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). Knowledge of federal, state, and private sources for contract and grant funds. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63694&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Postdoctoral Scholar - Webster",
      "description": "OPS Postdoctoral Scholar - Webster Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63694 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Postdoctoral Researcher in Genetics, Genomics, and Bioinformatics The Webster Lab in the Department of Biological Science at Florida State University invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher. Our lab investigates individual variation: we seek to understand why genetically identical individuals in a shared environment vary for both molecular and organismal phenotypes, and we then determine how genotype and environment can regulate this variation. We combine computational genomics, molecular biology, and experiments in Caenorhabditis elegans to address these questions. The successful candidate will help shape a project aligned with their interests and career goals. Projects may be fully computational or may combine bioinformatics with laboratory experiments. Funding for the position will be provided through either our lab's NSF CAREER award or startup funds, depending on the planned project. Responsibilities The postdoctoral researcher will analyze large genomic datasets, develop reproducible analysis pipelines, contribute to manuscripts and presentations, and collaborate with other members of the lab. The position requires thoughtful and efficient use of modern coding assistants as part of computational work, together with careful validation, documentation, and version control. Depending on the project and the candidate’s interests, responsibilities may also include designing and conducting experiments with C. elegans, mentoring junior researchers, and contributing to grant proposals. The position may be fully computational, or may be a split between computational and wetlab work; in either case, proficiency with bioinformatic analysis is a must. Qualifications A Ph.D. completed by the position’s start date in genetics, genomics, bioinformatics, molecular biology, evolutionary biology, or a closely related field Experience analyzing high-throughput sequencing data using bioinformatics Proficiency in at least one relevant programming language, such as R or Python Ability to work independently and collaboratively and to communicate research effectively Preferred Qualifications Experience working with C. elegans Experience with transcriptomic, epigenomic, or population-genomic sequencing data Experience developing reproducible computational workflows Interest in combining computational analysis with molecular or organismal experiments Helpful The lab is committed to supportive, individualized mentoring. The postdoctoral researcher and principal investigator will establish a mentoring plan and revisit it regularly through one-on-one meetings. Mentoring will include support for research independence, publishing, conference participation, fellowship and grant applications. Postdoctoral scholars have access to career-development programs, networking, travel awards, and other resources through FSU’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs . They may participate in the FSU Postdoctoral Association . Candidates interested in teaching may also pursue opportunities to serve as an instructor of record for a course, subject to departmental need and approval. Contact Info Questions may be directed to Amy Webster . Additional information about the lab is available here . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Compensation, mentoring, and professional development Salary will be commensurate with relevant postdoctoral experience and aligned with the current NIH NRSA postdoctoral stipend scale . The position also includes applicable FSU employee benefits. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Applicants should submit (1) a cover letter describing their research experience, interests, and career goals; (2) a curriculum vitae; and (3) contact information for two references. Review of applications will begin October 26 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is flexible, but ideally will be between January and July 2027. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63646&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Technician OPS",
      "description": "Technician OPS Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63646 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is pleased to announce the acceptance of qualified applications for the Computer Technician (OPS) position within Information Technology Services (ITS) . Responsibilities Providing excellent, responsive service to our college customers (faculty, staff and students) when they contact our office (walk in or call in); Handle simple technical issues; Assist more senior teammates with various projects, including personal computer and classroom technology support. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalency and some experience with customer service roles and supporting personal computers. Good basic knowledge of Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Office. Commitment to providing excellent customer service. Good communications skills. Prepared to work well in a team-oriented environment. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63664&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate in Research, 12 Month Salaried (Statistics)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate in Research, 12 Month Salaried (Statistics) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63664 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Statistics | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Statistics at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure-track Assistant in Research or Associate in Research faculty position in Biostatistics. The successful candidate will join one of the nation’s oldest and most reputable statistics departments and contribute to an established, growing biostatistics research program through collaborative biomedical, clinical, translational, and population health research across a comprehensive research university. The successful candidate will: Collaborate with investigators from FSU Health, the College of Medicine, and other interdisciplinary research programs and centers across FSU on the study design, conduct, analysis, and interpretation of research findings. Provide statistical expertise in the application of appropriate modern statistical and computational methods. Contribute to preparing and participating in grant applications, research protocols, manuscripts, presentations, and other scholarly products. Communicate statistical methods and findings effectively to collaborators from diverse scientific and clinical backgrounds. Promote rigorous and reproducible research through appropriate statistical research collaboration. Contribute to the Department’s interdisciplinary research initiatives and broader scholarly and research mission. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Biostatistics, Statistics, or a closely related quantitative field is required by the time of appointment. Candidates should demonstrate: Strong training in statistical methodology, data analysis, and proficiency in statistical programming software such as R, SAS, Python, or equivalent platforms. Demonstrated potential for effective collaboration in biomedical, clinical, translational, public health, or other interdisciplinary research settings. Strong written and oral communication skills, including the ability to explain statistical concepts to collaborators from other disciplines. Ability to manage multiple collaborative research projects and work effectively both independently and as part of interdisciplinary teams. Experience communicating and collaborating effectively with investigators from non-statistical disciplines. Contact Info For questions about our hiring process, please contact Pamela McGhee . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please apply by January 15, 2027. This position requires that you submit a statement on research and have at least three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63609&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Digital Humanities Librarian, 12 Month Salaried",
      "description": "Digital Humanities Librarian, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63609 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Libraries Responsibilities The Digital Humanities Librarian serves as the advanced technical lead for CreateFSU, the Libraries' academic web-hosting service, providing expert consultation and technical support for faculty and student digital scholarship initiatives. This position collaborates closely with the DRS team, the AI and Data Lab, and campus partners to advance digital research methodologies, expand access to emerging technologies, and support the university's mission of research excellence and student success. The successful candidate will help empower researchers and students to explore, create, and share new forms of scholarship while contributing to a vibrant and growing digital humanities community at FSU. Support Digital Scholarship and Research Innovation Serve as the advanced technical lead for CreateFSU and related web-hosting platforms, providing consultation, troubleshooting, and support for complex digital scholarship projects. Assist faculty, graduate students, and researchers in developing and sustaining digital humanities projects using a variety of publishing and web-based platforms. Develop and maintain technical documentation, tutorials, and user guides that support digital research and publishing initiatives. Advance Student Learning and Research Skills Collaborate with DRS colleagues to design and deliver workshops, instructional programming, and technical training through initiatives such as the Digital Research Incubator. Provide instruction in digital research methods, programming, data analysis, and related technologies, helping students and researchers build practical skills that support academic and professional success. Partner with faculty to integrate digital humanities tools, methodologies, and assignments into undergraduate and graduate curricula. Build Campus Partnerships Consult with faculty, students, and staff on digital research projects, scholarly communication, and emerging technologies. Foster collaborative relationships with partner units, including the Research Computing Center and the Interdisciplinary Data Humanities Initiative. Serve as a resource for campus digital scholarship efforts and contribute to strategic initiatives that enhance research capabilities across disciplines. Contribute to Professional Excellence Engage in ongoing professional development and scholarly activities related to digital humanities, digital scholarship, and academic librarianship. Participate in library, university, and professional service activities. Stay informed of emerging trends, technologies, and best practices that advance digital research and scholarship. Qualifications Master's degree from an ALA-accredited library and information science program; or Master's degree in a humanities discipline, digital humanities, or a closely related field with relevant technical experience. Demonstrated ability to independently learn and apply new technologies, software applications, programming languages, and web-based tools. Understanding of current research trends, emerging technologies, and methodological shifts in the digital humanities. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a commitment to public service and user-centered support. Strong collaborative mindset and adaptability in a fast-paced, evolving organizational environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing technical support, debugging, or administration for web-hosting platforms (e.g., WordPress, Reclaim Hosting). Proficiency in programming languages common to humanistic research, such as Python or R. Familiarity with web development technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) for site customization and troubleshooting. Demonstrated experience designing and delivering technical instruction, workshops, or academic presentations. Ph.D. in a humanities or related digital studies field. Other Information University Libraries seeks a collaborative and technically skilled Digital Humanities Librarian to help shape the future of digital scholarship, research innovation, and student learning. Located within the Office of Digital Research and Scholarship (DRS), this position provides an exciting opportunity to partner with faculty, researchers, and students on innovative digital humanities projects while helping develop technical skills and research capabilities that support academic success. Join us in advancing discovery, scholarship, and student success through the power of digital humanities and emerging technologies. At FSU Libraries, you will have the opportunity to: Collaborate with innovative faculty, researchers, and students on impactful digital scholarship projects. Help prepare students with the digital research and analytical skills needed for academic and career success. Work in a collaborative environment that values creativity, innovation, continuous learning, and professional growth. Contact Info Dr. Aaron Rodriguez , Director of Digital Research and Scholarship University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $60,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63657&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering-Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering-Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63657 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for teaching faculty positions in the field of Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in graduate courses and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to teach graduate-level classes (in-person and online), and have a strong interest in using technology in engineering education. Helpful The MAE Department currently has about 36 faculty, 200+ graduate students, ~1000 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $27M. We are starting our graduate programs (MS-Aero and MS-Mechanical) at the FSU Panama City (PC) campus. We expect the candidates to be part of our faculty at the FSU PC campus and to collaborate with our existing faculty at the Tallahassee campus. Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit our website Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint university is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at our independent campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Unnikrishnan Sasidharan Nair, Search Committee Chairperson, usasidharannair@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page teaching statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed teaching plan will connect with existing courses in the department and universities. A 1-page research statement (optional) Two selected publications for review (optional) The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information We are interested in candidates with backgrounds in Mechanical & Aerospace engineering who can teach graduate-level courses, including but not limited to Aerodynamics, Fluid Dynamics, Aerospace Propulsion, Aerospace Structures, Dynamics & Controls, and Mechanics & Materials. Other areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering will also be considered, particularly if they complement the department's existing strengths. The positions are at the Teaching Faculty I level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered for a higher rank. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on January 4, 2027. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63660&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Immigration Advisor",
      "description": "Immigration Advisor Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63660 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Center for Global Engagement Responsibilities This position will provide immigration-related services and advise international students enrolled in F-1 status. Serve as a Department of Homeland Security Designated School Official regularly submitting updates to the federal immigration (SEVIS) database to comply with regulatory reporting responsibilities and to authorize or recommend immigration benefits. Interpret and apply federal immigration regulations to support students in their maintenance of lawful F-1 status. Effectively use the Sunapsis database to ensure accurate immigration-related records. Assist and guide students with solving problems and identifying resources. Work closely with academic departments, university Human Resources, and other units throughout FSU. Engage in extensive and frequent communication by phone, Teams/Zoom, email and in-person with enrolled international students in F-1 status, other CGE team members, FSU faculty and staff, community, employers, and representatives of government agencies on issues related to federal F-1 immigration regulations (e.g. enrollment, graduation, transfer/change of level, employment authorization, extension of stay, etc.), general immigration laws that impact students in F-1 status (e.g. registration documentation, address reporting, international travel, change of status, etc.), and other state and federal policies. Help create supportive environment for international students. Work closely with academic departments, Admissions, Registrar, Student Finance, Division of Student Affairs departments, and other partners across campus. Hold multiple roles in FSU databases, with access to input and change visa codes, place and remove holds, view basic admissions information, student account information, student addresses, and student enrollment information, etc. Participate in the development and testing of new electronic forms developed by the Program Director for Data and Compliance, recommend updates to current forms and form communication, and provide feedback on data feed and data extract issues. Access daily the federal government immigration (SEVIS) database and Sunapsis to enter determinations regarding continuing eligibility for F-1 status, process employment authorizations (Curricular Practical Training) or recommendations (Optional Practical Training), update academic program changes, transfer immigration records to other U.S. institutions, and submit other required updates within regulatory reporting periods. Maintain accurate background information and documentation in Sunapsis to support the submitted SEVIS updates as required by regulations. Monitor daily auto-assigned cases in Sunapsis to identify immigration status issues and to review and process submitted electronic forms. Use Sunapsis communication tools to contact students regarding their cases to ensure consistent advising. Deliver regular Optional Practical Training workshops in person and via Zoom in rotation with other CGE advisors. Participate in new international student orientations each semester by giving presentations, checking students in, and/or guiding short tours. Play a role in the semesterly ACIREMA interactive simulation activity for the university community. Assist with developing and providing additional presentations and workshops for international students and the FSU community. Attend trainings offered by Undergraduate Advising, Human Resources, Research Compliance, and other areas. Contribute to CGE assessment efforts as needed. Participate in major CGE events and programs. Serve on DSA and/or CGE committees as needed. Provide back-up support to other advisors and to front desk. Participate in professional associations for international educators. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Applicant must be a U.S. citizen or permanent resident due to federal SEVIS database requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in international affairs, higher education, or closely related field. Experience as a Designated School Official and/or Alternate Responsible Officer using SEVIS regularly. Experience using Sunapsis, Terra Dotta, or other case management software. Ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining a high level of accuracy and efficiency. Experience presenting information in one-on-one, small group, and large group settings both in-person and online. Evidence of strong professional writing skills and ability to analyze complex information. Experience living, studying, or working abroad and knowledge of a second language. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting in the high $40,000’s to low $50,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Applicants must upload a cover letter when completing the online application. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applicants will begin on October 16, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61585&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain, College of Business)",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain, College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61585 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain | College of Business Responsibilities The Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems, and Supply Chain (BAISSC) at Florida State University’s Herbert Wertheim College of Business invites applications for a teaching faculty position (non-tenured track, 9 months salaried). The start date is August 2027. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in the areas of Business Analytics and Information Systems. Possible graduate level and/or additional course offerings may be available depending on qualifications. Qualifications An earned doctorate or other terminal degree from an accredited institution in a field closely related to Business Analytics or Information Systems is required. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience in areas such as Operations Management, Business Analytics, and/or Management Information Systems. Contact Info For inquiries regarding this position, please contact: Dr. Noyan Ilk Department Chair Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application materials include: 1) A letter of interest 2) Curriculum vitae 3) Three letters of reference This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will remain open until January 15, 2027. For priority consideration, please submit all application materials by November 15, 2026, when application reviews will begin. Applications received after this date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
