    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62755&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty - FNP Coordinator, 12 Month Salaried - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty - FNP Coordinator, 12 Month Salaried - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62755 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Join a nationally recognized leader in nursing education, known for research distinction and educational innovation. With simulation space in a brand new $126 million FSU Health building, $12 million to design a new building, and a transformative $10 million gift, the FSU College of Nursing is hiring additional faculty for strategic growth. Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire a collaborative educator to teach in our graduate program, based in Tallahassee, Florida (FL). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Actively work with the Assistant Dean for Graduate Program to develop and revise Graduate Curriculum. Assume an active role in recruiting prospective graduate students to the FNP (Family Nurse Practitioner) major; Review potential plans of study with prospective students. Maintain pertinent professional organization membership and assume leadership roles in professional organizations that support FNP practice and education. Teach Core Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) or FNP courses as assigned; assume lead responsibility for practicum courses within program. Conduct DNP and certificate FNP Program orientation activities. Oversee Objective Structured Clinical Evaluation (OSCE) within track. Work with Clinical Coordinator to recruit high-quality clinical preceptors. Manage student clinical rotations in conjunction with assigned clinical faculty. Work with the Assistant Dean for Graduate Program to forecast student enrollments in track courses. Work with Clinical Coordinator to execute PEPs, or preceptor forms/letters as needed. Review and verify clinical logs of DNP and certificate FNP students, providing student and faculty feedback, as appropriate. Review and monitor clinical hours for graduate students. Track certification requirements and results for Graduate Program. Evaluate transfer credits for FNP students in conjunction with the Assistant Dean. Complete and conduct FNP student annual review (May - June) and guide students through admission, matriculation and completion of major related courses. Complete education verification forms for certification. Other duties as assigned in the coordination of track-related activities as the lead faculty program track faculty member, such as but not limited to: supporting new faculty teaching in both didactic and practicum courses (orient to course syllabus, set up Simple syllabus as needed, orient students and relevant faculty to the track, track courses, and track-related activities) This role focuses on high-quality instruction in the graduate nursing program and supports the college’s mission to prepare practice-ready, compassionate nurse leaders. Faculty are expected to be actively engaged in teaching, student mentorship and academic service in a collaborative environment. For more information about our academic programs, visit our Academics page . Qualifications An academic doctorate (PhD, DNP) or highest-level terminal degree in nursing from an accredited institution is required, with eligibility for graduate faculty status. Non-nurse trained candidates will not be considered. Active FL Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) license; or licensed in another state with eligibility to obtain FL licensure within 30 days of hire. Two to three years of teaching experience in graduate nursing education. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of DNP education standards and AACN Essentials (2021). Experience with curriculum development, course coordination, or program evaluation Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work well with students, faculty, and staff at all levels within a collaborative environment. Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook or equivalent software. Experience supervising and training employees. Experience meeting project deadlines. Other Information This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. Contact Info Inquiries about the positions may be directed to Dr. Susan A Baker , Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In your application, please include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) including a listing of courses developed and taught Teaching Philosophy, not to exceed two pages Please do not include reference letters in your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. This position is being readvertised as open until filled. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63642&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Meteorology)",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Meteorology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63642 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science I College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean, and Atmospheric Sciences (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track, 12-month Teaching Faculty I position beginning Fall 2027 to teach undergraduate meteorology courses for majors and non-majors. We are particularly interested in candidates who can teach synoptic and broadcast meteorology. A full-time specialized faculty member in the Teaching Track (Teaching Faculty I, II, III) shall normally be assigned not less than 75% teaching responsibility and not more than 5% research responsibility, averaged over any academic year. This typically is represented as approximately eight 3-credit courses a year, with course reduction possible for substantial service roles such as academic advising or the TV Meteorology Program studio manager. Qualifications A Ph.D. or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in Meteorology or Atmospheric Science or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience is required, with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching. M.S. applicants with substantial teaching or broadcast meteorology experience post-degree are encouraged to apply. Other Information EOAS has 37 tenured/tenure-earning faculty, 3 teaching faculty, about 350 undergraduate students, about 100 graduate students, a student population, and grants undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. For additional information on EOAS research and FSU’s facilities and resources, please visit our website . The undergraduate meteorology degree program is large (typically 30 students each year) with a long and distinguished history dating back over 75 years. Contact Info Inquiries may be addressed to the chair of the search committee, Prof. Robert Hart . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching interest/philosophy, and contact information for three references who can provide letters of recommendation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin immediately. The deadline for receipt of applications is November 13, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63516&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Vocal Coaching, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Vocal Coaching, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63516 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music - Voice & Opera Area Responsibilities The qualified candidate will coach graduate voice majors in preparation for degree recitals and opera productions and will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to mentoring students. The candidate will also teach appropriate vocal-related courses in undergraduate and graduate sequences, including diction and song literature. Musical collaboration for faculty recitals will be expected. Additional responsibilities may include instructing graduate collaborative piano students; serving as Music Director of Opera Workshop; mentoring Opera Graduate Assistants; and contributing to other instructional and artistic activities appropriate to the candidate’s experience and expertise. Qualifications Candidate will have completed a doctoral degree in collaborative piano or a master's degree with equivalent professional experience with a record of achievement as an actively performing, collaborative artist. Knowledge of and experience in working as a vocal coach with professional proficiency in English, French, German and Italian lyric diction is required. Candidate must have experience coaching opera and vocal repertoire, across all major historical periods, at the post-secondary and/or professional level. The ideal candidate must be open to a range of musical styles and approaches to learning and teaching, recruitment, creative activity, and service. Preferred Qualifications Experience in Spanish, Russian and/or Czech is desired. The qualified candidate should demonstrate extensive experience performing and collaborating with vocal artists at the collegiate and/or professional levels. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills and demonstrated ability/interest in working in a collegial and mutually supportive environment is expected. Other Information FSU Opera encompasses three fully staged opera productions each year with orchestra; up to two outreach opera productions; curricular Opera Workshop and Opera Literature courses; MM programs in opera coaching and opera stage direction; and fully staged opera scenes programs. The qualified candidate will be an experienced and proficient opera coach and rehearsal accompanist and will contribute as a member of the FSU Opera team. Additional opportunities and responsibilities may be available depending on the candidate’s experience and expertise. The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist Other inquiries may be directed to the search committee chair as follows: Dr. Marcía Porter , Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application Materials: Cover letter, one to two pages CV Names and contact information for five references Links to performances of operatic and art song repertoire in a variety of languages, 20 to 30 minutes Vocal coaching video of the candidate coaching singer(s) from the piano, 20 to 30 minutes All videos and recordings must be from the last five years Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 15, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63616&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Interior Design, 9 Month Salaried - School of Design",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Interior Design, 9 Month Salaried - School of Design Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63616 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Design Responsibilities Florida State University invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track faculty position in Interior Design program at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. We seek a collaborative educator and scholar who will contribute to undergraduate and graduate education through innovative teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and student mentorship. The successful candidate will advance human-centered design, evidence-based inquiry, and creative and critical thinking while preparing students to address complex challenges in the built environment. Candidates should demonstrate expertise that complements and expands the program’s strengths and the ability to connect design inquiries with professional practice. We welcome contributions to interdisciplinary teaching and scholarship, graduate education, and the thoughtful integration of emerging technologies into design. Teach undergraduate and graduate studio, lecture, and/or seminar courses in interior design. Contribute expertise in Construction Documents, Construction Systems, Commercial Office and Hospitality Design, with flexibility to support other areas of the curriculum. Develop and sustain a program of research and/or creative scholarship, disseminate work through appropriate peer-reviewed or juried outlets, and pursue external funding opportunities. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students; advise graduate research and creative work; and chair or serve on thesis committees. Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation activities. Contribute to interdisciplinary collaboration and the integration of research, creative inquiry, and professional practice into teaching. Provide service to the academic unit, College, University, community, and profession, as appropriate to rank and assignment. Participate in relevant academic and/or professional organizations. Qualifications An earned master’s or doctoral degree in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field with substantial working experience Demonstrated teaching experience with Adobe Creative Cloud and Autodesk products, and familiarity with rendering & 3D visualization software (e.g., Enscape). Demonstrated ability to teach interior design studios and related courses effectively. Demonstrated ability to develop a sustained program of research and/or creative scholarship. Proficiency in design communication and the application of relevant design technologies in teaching, practice, and/or scholarship. Effective oral, written, and visual communication skills. Ability to collaborate with colleagues and support student learning and development. Candidates for appointment at the Assistant Professor rank should demonstrate promise in teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and service. Candidates for appointment at the Associate Professor rank should demonstrate a sustained record of teaching effectiveness, research and/or creative achievement, and service commensurate with appointment at that rank at Florida State University. Preferred Qualifications An MFA, M. Arch, PhD, or equivalent terminal degree in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field, completed by the appointment start date. Expertise in emerging design technologies (e.g., AI, VR, AR, etc.) and their thoughtful application to design education and inquiry (research/creative components). NCIDQ certification, architectural licensure or NCARB certification, and/or other relevant professional credentials. Teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Professional practice experience in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or related areas. Experience mentoring graduate students and supporting their thesis research or creative scholarship. Experience with interdisciplinary teaching, research, or collaborative design practice. Evidence of external funding activity or potential to develop externally supported projects. Familiarity with Council for Interior Design Accreditation standards and accreditation processes. Other Information The Interior Design Program in the School of Design at Florida State University emphasizes human-centered design, evidence-based design processes, and creative and critical thinking. The program prepares students to contribute to human health, safety, and well-being through the environments and experiences they design. Situated within the College of Fine Arts, the program offers opportunities to connect design education with broader artistic, scholarly, and interdisciplinary inquiry. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development of undergraduate and graduate education and help strengthen the program’s research and creative contributions. The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Contact Info Questions may be directed to Search committee chair, Daejin Kim , Ph.D., Associate Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. A letter of interest addressing qualifications, teaching expertise, and anticipated contributions to the program. A curriculum vitae. A teaching statement of one to two pages. A research and/or creative scholarship statement of one to two pages. A PDF portfolio containing 10–20 examples of research, creative, professional, and/or teaching-related work. Identify the applicant’s role in collaborative projects and distinguish student work from the applicant’s own work. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to MiKayla Jackson, Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. mjj22e@fsu.edu Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Review of applications will begin on December 15 and continue until the position is filled. The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63644&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Laboratory Assistant - Kopania (OPS)",
      "description": "Laboratory Assistant - Kopania (OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63644 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Dr. Emily Kopania's laboratory in the Department of Biological Scienc e at Florida State University (https://ekopania.github.io/ and https://www.bio.fsu.edu/). Our lab seeks to understand how selective pressures interact with developmental and functional constraints. We primarily do this by studying two different biological systems: (1) The evolution of vision in fish and (2) The evolution of reproduction in rodents. Our work integrates cutting-edge genomics and transcriptomics techniques with phylogenetic comparative approaches to understand molecular and trait evolution. Responsibilities The primary duties of this role include, but are not limited to, the following: Helping to set up a molecular genomics laboratory and fish husbandry facility. Performing molecular laboratory experiments. Examples include DNA and RNA extraction and library preparation, immunohistochemistry, and microscopy. General lab upkeep and organization, such as ordering supplies, scheduling, and maintaining supplies and equipment. Managing a fish (trout) facility through tasks such as regular feedings, health checks, and water quality monitoring. Mentoring and training others in laboratory techniques. Qualifications B.S. or B.A. degree (or higher) in the life sciences or related field. Exceptions may be made for students with laboratory research experience who are finishing their degrees this year. At least one year of experience in a biology laboratory. Proficiency with Microsoft Suite (Excel, Word, Teams) and Google Docs. A strong interest in evolutionary biology and genomics. Excellent time management, communication, and problem-solving skills. Strong ability to work with a team of students and researchers Preferred Qualifications Previous experience with molecular biology laboratory techniques. Previous experience working with animals in research settings, especially fish. Anticipated Salary Range Competitive salary commensurate with experience. Fringe benefits included. Ideal start date would be in October 2026 but is flexible based on candidate availability. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Please send your CV, a one-page statement describing your past research experience and interest in the position, and contact information for at least two references to Dr. Emily Kopania . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the position will remain open until filled. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . A full-time (40 hours/week), in-person research assistant position. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63829&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Business Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Business Operations Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63829 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Stoomps Center for Communities, Families, and Children The CFC Center was created by the Stoops Family Foundation, Inc. to generate and sustain translational knowledge development for effective policies, services, and usable research for the promotion of communities, families, and the children of Florida, the nation, and across the globe. Responsibilities Coordinate daily administrative operations and provide support to Center leadership, faculty, and staff. Process and monitor purchasing, travel, and other business transactions in accordance with University policies and procedures. Assist with budget tracking, financial reporting, expenditure monitoring, and reconciliation activities. Support operational planning and coordinate administrative needs with Center leadership, Program Managers, and University departments. Maintain accurate administrative and financial records, ensuring proper documentation and data entry. Serve as a point of contact for administrative inquiries and assist with resolving routine operational matters. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate will demonstrate exceptional attention to detail, strong customer service skills, and the ability to communicate effectively through both written and verbal communication. The ideal candidate will be able to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment, exercise critical thinking and sound judgment, and maintain a high level of professionalism while delivering quality service and support. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63831&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "IT Services Coordinator",
      "description": "IT Services Coordinator Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63831 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU’s Department of Northwest Regional Data Center (NWRDC) Responsibilities This position serves as a 2 nd shift weekdays. The incumbent in this position serves as the shift supervisor for the NWR-S Data Center. The incumbent is responsible for maintaining a working knowledge of the individual platforms, peripheral devices and facility infrastructure that support the Data Center. Incumbent will perform commands and monitor platforms and facility. The incumbent will perform within the rules, guidelines, and directions prescribed. Provide leadership, counseling, direction, performance feedback and development of career paths for staff. Evaluate employees using established criteria and maintain a consistent dialogue with them to keep them informed of their progress. This position involves frequent decision-making skills. Individual will be responsible for identifying problems and taking appropriate action to ensure timely and error-free service to the businesses supported by the Data Center. Establish or maintain a working knowledge of Data Center policies and procedures to include production control run schedules. Monitoring building security, computer room access. Maintain a working knowledge of mainframe platforms and hardware configurations. Maintain a working knowledge of facility and infrastructure. Maintain a working knowledge of Enterprise Network Monitoring Tools. Monitor all platforms for outstanding system messages, report issues and escalate as needed. Monitor the status of customer owned equipment and access to that equipment. Maintain Data Center logs and forms. Maintain a working knowledge of the ITSM Incident & Service Request processing tool in use. Create incident and service tickets, report issues and escalate as needed. Act as a liaison between applications, technical support, scheduling, and network staff to facilitate problem resolution during all abnormal circumstances. All personnel must attend/complete facility training as follows: Weekly load test (Switchgear) training a minimum of once a quarter if you are proficient with the systems or once a month for all new employees. Chiller (Chilled Water System) training once a quarter if employee is proficient with the system or once a month for new employee. All personnel must be able to react to an emergency on either of these systems within the specified time frames below: Switchgear issues within 5-minute time frame. Chilled water system within 10-minute time frame. All personnel must be able to communicate all issues clearly and concisely to facility staff in order to avert a facility shutdown. Act as Service Desk representative after hours and on weekends. Perform daily routines and related work as required. Perform other related duties as required. This position involves frequent decision-making skills. Individual will be responsible for identifying problems and taking appropriate action in order to ensure timely and error free service to the businesses being supported by the Data Center. Individual must be available to work overtime, and holidays as scheduled. Participates in approved professional development opportunities per NWRDC's policy. Professional development and training is defined as learning undertaken by the employee to maintain and advance their skills, knowledge and competencies, specifically as they relate and add value to the job and workplace. NWRDC provides support for a wide range of state and local government, as well as K-20 organizations across the State of Florida. These organizations are dependent on NWRDC in order to accomplish their missions. This requires NWRDC to maintain services 24/7, even during times of crisis or emergency. As such, all NWRDC staff are considered essential staff for operations of the State of Florida. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and four years' experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to four years. Preferred Qualifications Strong supervisory skills Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? Individual should be a self-starter, willing to work Monday – Friday 3:00pm – 11:30pm. Willing to work holidays and emergencies (off-shifts) when necessary, (These may occur at any time you are not scheduled to work). Individual should have at least 3 years minimum supervisory experience in a data center/operations setting. Report to duty during a natural disaster such as a hurricane, flood, or other emergencies. What is a typical day in this position? Individual will ensure that their team is performing all tasks associated with this shift and monitoring all aspects of the data center. Individual may have to sit alone for long periods of time but must stay alert. This position requires a certain level of activity such as bending, walking, lifting, and climbing stairs. What can I expect in the first 60-90 days? Individual will be provided a 16-week training program. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Anticipated schedule: Monday – Friday 3:00pm – 11:30pm Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63351&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Health & Human Services - Northwest Region, Health & Lifestyle (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Program Manager, Health & Human Services - Northwest Region, Health & Lifestyle (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63351 Location Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Florida State University’s College of Medicine has been awarded more than $19 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program to strengthen healthcare access and outcomes in rural Florida. The funding will support six new projects focused on critical needs including behavioral health, preventive care, food insecurity, telehealth, at-home care and healthcare workforce development. Through partnerships with communities and healthcare organizations across Northwest and Southwest Florida, FSU is working to bring innovative, practical solutions directly to rural communities and help close longstanding gaps in care. Responsibilities Manage project implementation: Oversee day-to-day activities for the Rural Health Transformation Program Initiative 9 across participating Northwest Florida counties and partner organizations. Develop and track workplans, timelines, milestones, and deliverables while addressing risks, barriers, and implementation challenges. Coordinate partners and stakeholders: Build and maintain relationships with healthcare organizations, community groups, public health partners, local governments, and other stakeholders. Facilitate advisory committee meetings, learning collaboratives, and stakeholder engagement activities to support collaboration and communication. Ensure compliance and program alignment: Ensure project activities meet program goals, contractual requirements, and university, state, federal, and funding agency policies. Coordinate contracts, subawards, consultants, and vendors while ensuring appropriate use of project resources. Monitor performance and quality improvement: Track project implementation and performance measures across all project components. Work with the Data Manager and project partners to review outcomes, identify opportunities for improvement, and support quality improvement and performance action plans. Manage budgets and resources: Monitor project budgets and expenditures, track resource utilization, and assist with budget planning and resource allocation to ensure funds are used appropriately and in accordance with funding requirements. Support reporting and dissemination: Coordinate progress reports for funding agencies and stakeholders and assist with presentations, summaries, policy briefs, and other program materials. Share project outcomes, successes, best practices, and lessons learned with stakeholders and at state and national forums. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience related to health and human services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to eight years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Reliable transportation, and a valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Georgia Arnold University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will be supporting Initiative 9 - Health & Lifestyle Northwest region, which is defined as Bay, Calhoun, Escambia, Franklin, Gadsden, Gulf, Holmes, Jackson, Jefferson, Leon, Liberty, Okaloosa, Santa Rosa, Wakulla, Walton, and Washington on the Rural Health Transformation Program Map . This position requires regular travel in support of program activities and responsibilities. Travel may occur within the employee’s assigned region and throughout the State of Florida, as needed. The frequency and location of travel may vary based on programmatic and operational needs. This job opening is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63643&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Professional Development Trainer/Bootcamp Instructor, ASCENT (Panama City Campus) (Multiple Vacancies) (Part-time, OPS)",
      "description": "Professional Development Trainer/Bootcamp Instructor, ASCENT (Panama City Campus) (Multiple Vacancies) (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63643 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department ASCENT - Office of Professional Engagement and Learning (OPEL) Florida State University is one of the nation’s top 25 public universities and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the sparkling waters of the Gulf. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ Responsibilities Providing classroom, online, or hybrid instruction in professional development and bootcamp formats. Fulfilling all contractual obligations during the term. Delivering training sessions aligned with pre-approved curricula and industry standards. Preparing thoroughly for each session and adhering to schedules. Leveraging modern teaching technologies, including learning management systems (LMS) and web-conferencing tools. Engaging learners actively, providing timely responses to questions and offering support or referrals when necessary. Collaborating with ASCENT staff to ensure seamless delivery and high-quality learner experiences. Assisting in the development and refinement of training content, as needed. Maintaining accurate records of attendance, grades, and evaluations, as applicable. Completing annual compliance training and adhering to university policies. Performing additional duties as assigned by the OPEL Program Manager. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Relevant industry certifications, coupled with two or more years of field experience. Preferred Qualifications Proven expertise in the subject areas being taught (e.g., technology, business, healthcare, etc.). Certifications in relevant tools or technologies (e.g., cybersecurity, IT, programming languages, project management, etc.). Post-secondary teaching or training experience preferred. Evidence of ongoing professional development through education, certifications, or other activities. Proficiency with teaching technologies, including LMS platforms, lecture-capture tools, and synchronous online engagement software. Strong communication and interpersonal skills with demonstrated ability to engage others. Contact Info Heidi Gentry University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The position is anticipated to begin in Fall 2026. This position requires a flexible schedule for trainings and occasional classes that start outside normal business hours. This position may be on location at any of the eight counties of the panhandle region. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63593&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant State Climatologist, 12 Month Salaried (Florida Climate Center)",
      "description": "Assistant State Climatologist, 12 Month Salaried (Florida Climate Center) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63593 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Climate Center | Center for Ocean-Atmospheric Predication Studies (COAPS) | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The selected candidate will be involved in the day-to-day operations of the Florida Climate Center, especially as it pertains to outreach and communication. This position will serve as a key member of the Center for Ocean-Atmospheric Prediction Studies (COAPS) outreach team and help identify, plan, and participate in a variety of events and opportunities. Limited travel to outreach events and workshops may be required. Responsibilities include: Providing climate data and services to citizens, private businesses, and government agencies in the State of Florida. Duties involve responding to inquiries about climate and weather via phone and email. Independently utilizing all resources available to answer questions and formulate data, products, and reports to meet the needs of the customer. Developing and disseminating regular climate products and reports, and maintaining a suite of web-based climate data products in response to needs and gaps. Serving as a liaison between the Florida Climate Center and our partners in climate services at the National Centers for Environmental information, Southeast Regional Climate Center, other state climate offices, and the National Weather Service. Performing research-related tasks as opportunities arise or as driven by public demand and in support of other projects/grants in place at COAPS. This could include independent research projects assigned by the Director of the Florida Climate Center, as well as providing data and technical support for research projects from undergraduate students, graduate students, summer interns, and faculty. Leading outreach/educational presentations and experiments related to climate and weather information in classroom as well as informal settings. Creating, editing, and distributing routine climate reports and newsletters. Managing and providing content to social media accounts for the Florida Climate Center. Qualifications A master's degree from an accredited institution in the field of Meteorology or a related science is required. A bachelor’s degree in Meteorology or related field with a minimum of two years of experience in the field of Meteorology/Climatology/Climate Services or in Science Education/Outreach/Communication may also be considered. This position will be hired at the rank of Assistant in Research. The selected candidate must also possess: A friendly and helpful professional demeanor and be able to work well independently as well as with a variety of groups including other scientists, the general public, and stakeholder groups, such as educators, practitioners, school-aged children, etc. Ability to prepare publication-quality graphics and maps, have basic web and programming skills, strong organizational skills, good oral and written communication, and the ability to write on technical subjects and make them understandable for non-scientists. Experience with data analysis, including basic knowledge of and/or the ability to learn computer programming and statistical analysis software, such as Python, R, HTML, SASS, GIS, or Matlab, as well as some research experience, is preferred. Contact Info For more details, please contact Dr. Emily Powell . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a state funded part-time position (0.50 FTE, 20 hours per week). Subject to the availability of future grant funding, the position may increase up to full-time (1.0 FTE). Applications review will begin November 13, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63628&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Reading Education or Special Education",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Reading Education or Special Education Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63628 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences and the Florida Center for Reading Research Responsibilities Candidates will be expected to maintain a rigorous grant writing and research program, teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in their program, train doctoral students, and participate in university governance commensurate with rank. Qualifications Ph.D. in Reading Education, Special Education, or related field Demonstrated evidence of rigorous research productivity Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching and training Demonstrated commitment to continued grant-funded research and scholarly productivity Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to and evidence of developing doctoral students Demonstrated evidence of (or potential for) an externally funded, independent research program A quality program of research related to reading and/or writing development, assessment, instruction, intervention, or related topic areas (emerging at the assistant rank, established at the associate rank) Teaching experience in preschool through grade 12 settings Other Information The School of Teacher Education (STE) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences (Anne’s College) and the Florida Center for Reading Research (FCRR) at the Florida State University invite applications for a nine-month, tenured or tenure-earning assistant or associate professor of Reading Education or Special Education. The position will involve teaching, research, and service within STE, and will include a joint appointment with FCRR. The position carries a reduced teaching assignment with correspondingly high expectations for research productivity. The successful candidate will have a tenure home in one of two majors within STE: Reading Education or Special Education. These majors work closely together in STE and FCRR, so a collaborative orientation is desired. The candidate will be expected to maintain a rigorous grant writing and research program, including competitive externally funded research grants. The candidate will also teach undergraduate, masters, and/or doctoral level classes within their program, and train doctoral students through active participation in their research program. The candidate will also be expected to participate in university governance in the department, college, and FCRR, at a level that is commensurate with their rank. The candidate will join an interdisciplinary group of colleagues and students at STE, Anne’s College, and FCRR. Drawing from multiple disciplines, FCRR investigates all aspects of reading and reading-related skills across the lifespan. Through rigorous and robust research, innovation, and engagement, FCRR advances the science of reading to improve learning and achievement from birth through adulthood. Meanwhile, Anne’s College advances society and enriches our community through support and education, while enhancing the quality of life of all our students, faculty and staff. Through meaningful collaborations, commitment to public scholarship, and integration of research, practice and policy, Anne’s College addresses America’s urgent education challenges in the innovative manner characteristic of FSU. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Sonia Cabell , Ph.D., Sigmon Endowed Professor and Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a CV, a cover letter detailing how they meet the required and preferred qualifications, a sample publication, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin 10/26/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. The anticipated start date is August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63604&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director, FSU Real Estate Center - Herbert Wertheim College of Business",
      "description": "Director, FSU Real Estate Center - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63604 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate and Legal Studies - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Advisory Board Management The Director leads the development and implementation of the objectives and strategic goals of the FSU Real Estate Center. Acts as the highly visible, senior external-facing leader and chief liaison to real estate industry personnel, employers, and alumni. Leverages an established industry network to expand opportunities for the Center. Manages the Center’s Executive Advisory Board, including directing Board communications and meetings, identifying and cultivating prominent industry leaders for new membership, assisting Board subcommittees, and reporting to the Board at its biannual meetings. Industry Engagement and Professional Events Provides the framework, strategic vision, and guidance for the Center’s professional events and activities, ensuring they serve as premier networking and talent pipeline opportunities. Oversees the annual TRENDS conference, the FSU-Kislak Market Strategy Forums, the Evan Jennings Speaker Series, the Real Deal & Entrepreneurs Series, and any future forums designed to advance the preeminence of the real estate program. Collaborates with faculty and external stakeholders to ensure programming reflects current industry trends, technologies, and market opportunities. Student Success and Career Pathways Responsible for connecting students in the real estate program with internships, mentorships, industry projects, and full-time career pathways through strategic employer partnerships. Coordinates the Center’s support of student activities, including the FSU Real Estate Society. Directs the Center’s program manager and other staff in the awarding of fellowships, travel grants, and administrative assistance for student participation in corporate tours, case competitions, networking opportunities, mentoring, and other experiential learning activities. Center Administration and Operation s Supervises Center staff and oversees the Center’s day-to-day administrative and financial operations. Coordinates Center communications with alumni, Executive Board members, sponsors, employers, students, and faculty. Ensures compliance with applicable University and State of Florida policies and requirements. Program Advocacy and Brand Management Serves as the primary external face of the Real Estate Center to industry leaders and professional organizations to articulate the successes and objectives of the Program, its faculty, and its students. Works with the College’s PR & marketing team to develop branding and messaging that elevates the Center’s national reputation. Assures that the FSUREC brand, mission, products, and services are consistently presented in a strong, positive image to relevant stakeholders. Donor Stewardship and Development Collaboration Acts as a subject-matter expert and strategic partner to the College’s development, engagement, business development, and career services teams to support fundraising, sponsorship, employer, executive education, and alumni/donor engagement efforts. Identifies and develops corporate sponsorship opportunities for Center programs and activities. Accompanies gift officers on strategic visits to provide programmatic vision, assisting in the cultivation and stewardship of employer and donor partners to enhance student, faculty, and Center resources. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to administrative services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and ten years of experience related to administrative services? (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated record of strategic leadership and partnership development, supported by a robust, existing network of commercial real estate professionals, employers, and industry leaders. Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder initiatives, professional events, and program budgets. An advanced degree in business, real estate, finance, planning, or a related field is highly desired. Six or more years of professional experience in commercial real estate development, commercial brokerage, investment, or related financial services. Experience working with students, faculty, and staff in a higher education setting. Professional credentials in real estate, planning, or finance are strongly advantageous. Contact Info J. Bradley Karl , PhD Chair, Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate and Legal Studies Dr. William T. Hold/The Alliance's Program in Risk Management and Insurance University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63502&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Jazz Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Jazz Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63502 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate-level jazz trumpet students, and supervise graduate teaching assistants. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio Serve on doctoral and master’s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include teaching courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Qualifications A doctoral degree in a related field or a master’s degree with equivalent professional experience is required at the time of appointment. The successful candidate will: Hold a record of successful university-level teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Other Information The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist For questions regarding the position, please contact Rodney Jordan , Professor of Jazz Bass and Coordinator of Jazz and Music Industry University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application Materials: Cover Letter, CV, List of Links, etc. Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 18th, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63500&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music Therapy, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Music Therapy, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63500 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teaches undergraduate and graduate-level courses in Music Therapy or related areas. Courses will be selected from current area offerings and/or implemented in the candidate's area of expertise. Supervises clinical music therapy experiences. Directs doctoral and master's-level committees. Conducts research and scholarly activities related to their interests and areas of expertise. Engage in recruitment of outstanding students. Develop and maintain community partnerships. Participates in university and professional service activities appropriate to rank. Qualifications Academic doctorate or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in Music Therapy or related area. Credentialing through the Certification Board for Music Therapists (MT-BC) is required. Minimum of five years of full time (or equivalent) clinical experience as an MT-BC is also required. A record of successful university-level teaching experience. Demonstrated excellence in clinical musicianship as a practicing professional. Experience as a clinical supervisor. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with substantial clinical and supervision experience, and who hold the NICU-MT and/or other specializations. A record of ongoing research/scholarly activity is also preferred. Other Information The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist Other inquiries may be directed to the search committee chair as follows: Dr. Lori Gooding , Associate Professor of Music Therapy and Co-Coordinator of Music Education & Music Therapy University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Each item below should be uploaded as a PDF to the Additional Documents section of the online application: One to two-page cover letter Curriculum vitae A copy of scholarly writing that clearly reflects your research focus and direction such as a refereed published article, an in-press article, or a doctoral-level scholarly paper Link to a 20-minute video of the applicant teaching Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link 2) Click the My References link 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by October 20th, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62416&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Ascension Bay Internal Medicine) College of Medicine",
      "description": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Ascension Bay Internal Medicine) College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62416 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, COM Residency Program Administration Responsibilities The Program Director oversees the Internal Medicine Residency Program (“IM Program” or “Program”) under the guidance of the Designated Institutional Official (DIO). The Program Director handles the general management, curriculum development, hiring, and teaching and mentoring of the Program. The Program Director sets the strategic vision of the Program and ensures its standards, quality, and reputation. The Program Director is expected to support the collaboration of the IM Program with physician practices and hospital clinical services in a way that improves value and quality, and that fosters a positive environment for professional practice and medical education. The Program Director will also work in collaboration with the program leadership to ensure outstanding educational offerings within Ascension Sacred Heart Bay Hospital. Clinical Teaching and Supervision of Residents Core Program Clinical Teaching Clinical Practice in Internal Medicine or applicable Subspecialty General Administration Graduate Medical Education (GME) Committees/Meetings GME Lecturing/Teaching Conferences GME Recruiting/Interviewing GME Research/Scholarly Activity Resident Evaluation/Monitoring Program Evaluation Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Valid FL medical license, or licensed in another state with the ability to obtain FL licensure. Must be board certified in Internal Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM). Must have a minimum of three years of faculty and administrative experience in an ACGME accredited internal medicine residency program. Preferred Qualifications Effective professional management skills, including the ability to plan, organize and schedule work in an efficient and productive manner, focusing on key priorities and meeting deadlines. Outstanding interpersonal, leadership, mentoring and teaching skills. A strong work ethic and desire to participate in a team-oriented, performance-driven health system. Ability to communicate with others in a clear, understandable, and professional manner in person, on the phone, electronically, and in writing. Ability to build and lead high-performing teams; must be able to provide clear and accurate direction and guidance. Strong administrative and team building skills. Other Information Ascension Sacred Heart Bay – Panama City, FL As part of Ascension, the largest non-profit health system in the U.S. and the world’s largest Catholic health system: Sacred Heart was founded by the Daughters of Charity in 1915. While our technology has improved dramatically, and the buildings have grown and expanded, our commitment to the mission remains steadfast: to provide excellent health care to all people, with special attention to the poor and vulnerable. Sacred Heart Health System includes hospital campuses in Pensacola, Miramar Beach, Panama City, and Port St. Joe, Florida, as well as The Studer Family Children’s Hospital at Sacred Heart, Northwest Florida’s only children’s hospital and Sacred Heart Medical Group, the largest network of primary care and specialty physicians in Northwest Florida. The 47-million-dollar renovation of Bay Medical after Hurricane Michael is in process and aims to create a facility with 200 private rooms. The improvements include major upgrades to information technology and creation of new space for physician offices and other services, including the laboratory, imaging and pharmacy. Bay offers an accredited Stroke Center, a Level II Trauma Center, which provides 24-hour emergency care for life-threatening injuries and illnesses, and emergency services located at the main hospital as well as a freestanding emergency center on Panama City Beach. Helpful The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape the program in their vision and recruit core faculty. Candidates with recent scholarly activity such as peer reviewed funding, publication of original research or review articles in peer-reviewed journals, chapters in textbooks, publication or presentation of case reports or clinical series at scientific society meetings, or participation in national committees or educational organizations are highly encouraged to apply. Contact Info Jessee Graham: jjgraham@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Faculty Information This faculty position is jointly affiliated with Florida State University (FSU) and Ascension Sacred Heart. Appointment is contingent upon the successful completion of all onboarding and employment requirements of both institutions. These requirements include, but are not limited to: a comprehensive credentialing process through Ascension Sacred Heart Medical Staff Office, background screening, professional reference checks, drug screening, and submission of a self-query report from the National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB). Please note that Ascension Sacred Heart credentialing process may take up to 90 days from the date the offer is accepted. Final appointment and the ability to initiate clinical responsibilities are contingent upon the approval of medical staff membership and clinical privileges by Ascension Sacred Heart. Further details regarding onboarding and credentialing processes will be provided during the interview and offer stages. Additional list of Ascension Sacred Heart Program Director Requirements . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a clinical/non-tenure earning role, and rank is commensurate with experience. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63607&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Chemical Oceanography/Aquatic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Chemical Oceanography/Aquatic Chemistry) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63607 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science l College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Chemical Oceanography / Aquatic Chemistry. We seek candidates whose research centers on aquatic chemical processes and biogeochemical cycling. Research areas of interest include, but are not limited to, the inorganic carbon system, ocean gas exchange, isotope geochemistry, nutrient cycling, chemical tracers of ocean circulation, aquatic / marine pollution, and modeling of chemical and biogeochemical processes in aquatic / marine systems. The appointee is expected to contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in Oceanography and Environmental Science, as well as to supervise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students in research and creative activities. The faculty member would support core instruction in chemical oceanography while developing advanced courses in specialized areas such as biogeochemical cycles, aquatic geochemistry, isotope geochemistry, and aquatic / marine pollution. The successful candidate would develop a vigorous externally funded research program focused on aquatic / marine chemical processes and biogeochemical cycling. Qualifications Candidates must hold a Doctoral degree or the highest degree appropriate in Oceanography / Environmental Science or a related discipline. Other Information EOAS is housed in a recent building (2020) with state-of-the-art facilities and laboratories, has approximately 35 tenure-track faculty and 100 graduate students, and offers undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. In addition to collaborations with other faculty within EOAS, the appointee can expect collaborations with colleagues at the Center for Ocean-Atmosphere Prediction Studies and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory. For additional information on EOAS and FSU’s resources, please check our website . Contact Info For any inquiries, please, reach out to search committee chair Dr. Robert Spencer . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Required application materials include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statements on research and teaching interests Contact information for three references to provide letters of recommendation Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63605&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Academic Affairs – Associate/Full Professor or Teaching Faculty II/III Rank - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Associate Dean for Academic Affairs – Associate/Full Professor or Teaching Faculty II/III Rank - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63605 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs serves in a leadership position, overseeing the operations of the Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) in the College. Leadership & Oversight Supervising, assigning areas of responsibility, and evaluating all faculty and staff within the Academic Affairs unit (approximately 17 faculty and staff). Overseeing the unit’s financial planning and budgeting activities. Student Affairs Serving as the Academic Dean for all student-related processes, which includes, but is not limited to: Advising students, faculty, and chairs regarding Grade Appeals and General Grievance processes. Advising the College Student Leadership Committee (SLC). Academic Affairs Serving as the Academic Dean and the College liaison for University-level entities, including the Office of Accreditation and Quality Assurance, the Office of Institutional Performance and Assessment, the Office of Faculty Development and Advancement, Undergraduate Studies and the Graduate School. Serving on multiple committees as the College representative for academic affairs. Maintaining the College Degree Program Inventory (DPI) and Certificate Program Inventory (CPI) with FSU IR. Assisting academic programs with new degree, major, and certificate proposals. Working closely with chairs, faculty, academic staff, and students regarding the College and FSU graduate and undergraduate policies and procedures. Overseeing the College curriculum committee and associated curriculum proposal process. Approving all Graduate Faculty Status, Graduate Teaching Status, and Co-Directive applications. Recruitment, Admissions, & Enrollment Management Data Overseeing all College academic affairs data processes, including analysis and reporting. Coordinating annual student Program Satisfaction Surveys. Assisting with design and maintenance of the College Data SharePoint site. Accreditation & State Program Approval (Office of Quality Assurance) Serving as FSU’s Florida Department of Education Liaison for all educator preparation programs (Anne’s College, Panama City, Fine Arts, and Music). Maintaining curriculum, policies, and procedures for all FLDOE approved educator preparation programs. Working with nationally accredited programs through assisting in the design and full implementation of student learning outcome assessment systems. Working Environment Promoting methods for communicating policies and procedures to faculty and academic staff; Supports department academic staff in all areas of academic affairs. Maintaining a congenial and collaborative relationship with all departments and academic support units within the College. Teaching Department responsibilities are limited to teaching and advising doctoral students. Teaching responsibilities equivalent to one course per academic year in the fall or spring semester for tenure-track candidates or two courses per academic year for specialized faculty candidates. Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in a discipline related to one of the academic units in the College. Demonstrated success in research and/or teaching, depending on the type of faculty line (tenured/tenure-earning or specialized teaching) sought. Prior experience in academic leadership at the program, center, institute, department, or college level. Ability to analyze data and make data-informed decisions. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with state-approved and/or nationally accredited academic programs. Prior experience developing new academic degree programs. Other Information The Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for an Associate Dean for Academic Affairs position to start in July or August of 2027. For external candidates, the faculty rank (tenure-track associate/full professor or specialized teaching faculty II/III) associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. The Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) is the representative office for the academic dean of the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences. OASIS strives to provide students, staff, and faculty, with the tools and support needed for student success. OASIS serves as the central repository for all student records, monitors required academic milestones, provides academic advising and support for undergraduate students, collaborates with academic departments to provide academic support for graduate students, and serves as the primary liaison between current students and the Office of the Registrar, the Division of Undergraduate Studies, and The Graduate School. OASIS directly manages the undergraduate admission process and provides support to academic departments in the admission of graduate students. Additionally, OASIS works with educator preparation programs throughout the university to coordinate internship placements and field-based experiences with PK-12 schools and students. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Toby Park-Gaghan , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of academic affairs leadership philosophy. Transcripts, work samples (such as journal articles or teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. A 9-month versus 12-month appointment will be dependent on the selected candidate's rank and program. Review of candidates will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63592&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63592 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Dance Responsibilities The Florida State University School of Dance invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Open Rank Faculty in Dance with expertise in Dance Science, Dancer Health and Wellness, and evidence-informed approaches to dancer training. We seek a collaborative scholar, educator, and mentor whose work bridges scientific inquiry, embodied practice, and creative exploration in ways that advance the preparation and well-being of dancers. Situated within our nationally recognized Dancer Training Program, this position offers a distinctive opportunity for an individual whose expertise may span areas such as applied science, performance research, pedagogy, somatic practices, rehabilitation, conditioning, creative scholarship, or interdisciplinary inquiry, while maintaining a clear commitment to optimizing dancer development through research-informed practice. The successful candidate will join a dynamic community of faculty, staff, and students dedicated to innovation, excellence, and the evolving future of dancer training. Teaching The successful candidate will contribute to the School's nationally recognized Dancer Training Program through teaching that reflects expertise in dance science, dancer health and wellness, and evidence-informed approaches to training. Teaching courses such as Dance Conditioning, Dance Kinesiology, Science of Dance Training, Dance Coaching, Research in the Dance Sciences, and related topics. Contributing specialized instruction in areas aligned with the candidate's expertise, such as Pilates, Gyrotonic, Yoga, Strength and Conditioning, Somatic Practices, Motor Learning, Injury Risk Management, Rehabilitation-Informed Training, Dance Technique, and other movement-based practices. Developing innovative courses and learning experiences that integrate scientific inquiry, embodied practice, creative exploration, and emerging approaches to dancer development. Research and Creative Scholarship The successful candidate will maintain an active research and/or creative scholarship agenda that advances the preparation, performance, health, and well-being of dancers. Conducting research related to dancer health, wellness, performance optimization, conditioning, pedagogy, injury risk management, motor learning, and related areas in the dance sciences. Disseminating scholarship through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and other professional activities and venues with national and international reach. Engaging in applied, practice-based, and creative forms of inquiry that connect research with studio, classroom, laboratory, rehearsal, or performance settings. Contributing to the continued evolution of the dance sciences through interdisciplinary, collaborative, and innovative approaches to research and artistic practice. Service The successful candidate will contribute to the shared governance and mission of the School of Dance through service to the program, university, and profession. Serving on the Dance Conditioning and Wellness Committee and supporting initiatives within the School's Movement Training Laboratory. Contributing expertise to programs and initiatives that promote dancer health, wellness, and performance excellence. Participating in School, College, and University governance through committee work and other service assignments determined through faculty governance processes and in consultation with the Chair. Engaging in professional service activities that support the broader fields of dance science, dancer training, and higher education. Mentoring and Student Development The successful candidate will mentor undergraduate and graduate students as artists, scholars, researchers, and movement practitioners. Advising students pursuing interests in the dance sciences, dancer health and wellness, movement training, performance coaching, or related fields. Mentoring student research, creative scholarship, and practice-based inquiry. Guiding students in the application of evidence-informed approaches to performance preparation, training, recovery, and injury-risk reduction. Supporting students' professional development and preparation for careers in academic, artistic, clinical, research, or interdisciplinary settings. Contributing to an environment of student success through mentoring that extends across teaching, scholarship, service, and community engagement. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization from an accredited institution in one of the dance sciences or a related field with an emphasis on working with dancers. Evidence of scholarly, creative, or applied research activity related to dancer development, health and wellness, performance optimization, pedagogy, movement training, or closely related areas. Demonstrated ability to contribute to a collaborative academic environment and to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students in advancing initiatives related to dancer training, health, and wellness. Demonstrated commitment to evidence-informed practice and the integration of research, embodied knowledge, and teaching. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching courses related to the dance sciences, dancer health and wellness, movement training, conditioning, kinesiology, performance preparation, pedagogy, coaching, or related fields. Experience teaching, coaching, training, or facilitating movement-based practices such as Pilates, Gyrotonic, Yoga, Strength and Conditioning, Somatics, Motor Learning, Injury Risk Management, Rehabilitation-Informed Training, Dance Technique, or other approaches that support dancer development and well-being. Active research, creative scholarship, or applied professional practice that advances understanding of healthy and effective dancer training. Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students in research, creative inquiry, professional practice, or career pathways related to dance science, dancer health and wellness, and movement training. Demonstrated ability to bridge scientific inquiry, embodied practice, and artistic exploration in teaching, scholarship, or professional work. Familiarity with quantitative, qualitative, mixed-methods, and/or practice-based research approaches relevant to dancer training and performance, including experience with small-N and within-subject research designs. Other Information The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Montgomery Hall is one of the best developed dancer training facilities in the nation. The Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) is an internationally recognized dance choreographic research center and part of the School of Dance. This unique and visionary institute brings a steady stream of prominent and emerging dance artists to campus to create and develop the work that the rest of the world will experience in years to come. Add to this mix an esteemed faculty and talented, highly motivated students, and it is easy to see why we are excited for what is to come. Contact Info Search Committee Chair: Professor Gwen Welliver University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are required to submit: Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three references. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applicants will begin on December 1, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63596&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Professor & Director, 9 Month Salaried - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Professor & Director, 9 Month Salaried - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63596 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Provide leadership and strategic direction for all academic programs in the School Lead and enhance the School’s strategic efforts for research productivity and excellence Lead the effort for identifying the major priorities of the School, including the combined BS/MS pathways in teacher education, and other graduate programs (e.g., PhD and master’s) Align the School’s strategic planning goals with the strategic plans of the University and the College Manage budgetary, personnel, and other departmental resources Foster and maintain a supportive environment for all faculty, staff, and students in the School Provide leadership and direction for creating an environment of transparency and open communication within the School Enhance the rigor and quality of research in the School, as well as the opportunities for PhD students Collaborate with the Director of the Florida Center for Reading Research and the Learning Systems Institute to continue developing productive research partnerships that promote the work of faculty in the department Lead efforts to build relationships within and outside the University that lead to the betterment of the College, and the well-being of the community and the region Qualifications Earned doctorate from one of the educational disciplines found within the School, or a closely-related field. A record of scholarly accomplishments consistent with the rank of full professor with tenure; exceptionally qualified candidates may also be considered for the Mack and Effie Campbell Distinguished Professorship. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in academic leadership, including budgetary oversight and management Broad research knowledge and experience at Research 1 universities—to understand, guide, and communicate with faculty working in different fields within various paradigms and methodologies Experience as a leader for faculty members’ professional development and growth. Experience with building and maintaining relationships with K-12 and community agency field partners and field-placement management Demonstrated commitment to faculty development and advancement Other Information The Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a Professor and Director of the School of Teacher Education. The College encourages applications from visionary leaders committed to education and its role in maximizing human potential. Reporting to the Dean of the College, the Director is responsible for the overall success of the School, its students, and its faculty and staff. The School of Teacher Education is committed to high quality personnel preparation programs; service to the state of Florida; and high-quality scholarly research in elementary education, early childhood education, reading/language arts, second language education, special education, blindness and low vision, science education, math education, social science education, English education, and related areas. The School strives to provide undergraduate and graduate students with world-class training in teaching, research, and professional development. Through the guidance and mentorship of faculty, students graduate to serve as educational leaders who will contribute to the betterment of a pluralistic, global society in the context of the state of Florida's needs for an educated, global-minded citizenry. In addition to mentoring and preparing the next generation of educators, faculty engage in a wide range of research activities. Faculty work routinely appears in prestigious publications and is cited by peers. Furthermore, faculty receive support from a robust Office of Research to pursue research opportunities, professional awards, and more. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Dr. Alysia Roehrig , Search Committee Chair Questions regarding the application submission system and process should be directed to the application coordinator: Jania Kadar , Sr. Administrative Specialist University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted prior to notifying applicants), and a cover letter of no more than four pages that articulates the candidate’s experience and vision for the School as related to: (1) leadership, innovation, and strategic partnerships; (2) research; and (3) teaching. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin October 31, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position has a proposed start date of July 1, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62745&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, Level II-IV (Magnet Science & Technology - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)",
      "description": "Research Engineer, Level II-IV (Magnet Science & Technology - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62745 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America’s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities Responsible for mechanical design applying standard engineering practices, procedures, and criteria in designing complex high field magnet assemblies at the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory. Engineering Design & Analysis Responsible for selecting standard engineering techniques, procedures, and criteria in designing complex magnets. Evaluate requirements and constraints of magnets, designed to meet scientific or research needs, and create mechanical designs to accommodate them according to their applied loads. Perform structural analyses to designed hardware and fasteners. Read and understand technical drawings including geometric dimensioning and tolerancing. System Design & Development Directs conceptual design, detailed system design, and preparation of engineering drawings/documents of magnet systems using 3D CAD and may also include software such as Autodesk Inventor, Solid Works, Pro-Engineer, etc. Design from engineering prototype to final system using technology development, fabrication process development, preparation of engineering documentation, and supply chain management. Testing, Fabrication & Quality Develop tooling and assist in building mechanical assemblies while applying quality controls and adhering to safe practices. Responsible for preparing, testing, and evaluating plans and specifications of magnets designed to meet scientific or research needs. Ensures the product quality meets the researchers needs. Develops unique methods and processes for technical tasks such as system assembly, performance testing and analysis of results. Project Coordination & Collaboration Interacts and coordinates with external users, researchers, and scientists in the development and implementation of projects. Assists group leaders in directing individual project/programs. In absence of group leaders may need to provide leadership decision making concerning acquisitions, staff and technical project details. Attend team meetings to discuss project testing needs and report test results. Conduct background research to help develop and define engineering requirements. Interact with other professional staff for test method development, and the design and construction of magnet systems. Laboratory Operations Perform general laboratory duties such as creating purchase requests, maintaining tools and equipment, and organizing and maintaining inventory. Research, Publications & Outreach Publish and/or present the results designs, testing, or other works in journals or conferences when appropriate. Participate in outreach activities and interact with numerous technical visitors from domestic and international laboratories and industries. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years of experience; or a high school diploma and seven years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Additional experience qualifies candidates for higher-level consideration (III–VI). Each level requires three additional years of experience. Helpful What you Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info Please contact Kayla West if you have questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Level II – Mid $60,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level III – Mid $70,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level IV – Mid $80,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63538&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Research, 9 Month Salaried - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Associate Dean for Research, 9 Month Salaried - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63538 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Research serves in a leadership position, overseeing the operations of the Office of Research in the College. Operations Supervising, assigning areas of responsibility, and evaluating faculty, clinical and administrative staff within the Office of Research unit (approximately 15 faculty and staff), as appropriate Overseeing the Office of Research (OoR) operations, including but not limited to: Identifying and implementing effective grant development activities and proposal tracking systems for efficient operation within the OoR Supervising the administration of all grants related activities effectively and with a commitment to the highest quality of customer service for faculty and staff Creating and implementing innovative programs expanding research activities Tracking and supporting grant activity, using a variety of analytical tools (e.g., Academic Analytics) to analyze proposal submissions, grant awards, journal article publications, journal article citations, and honorific awards Maintaining fiscal responsibility for the OoR budget, external fund sources affiliated with the OoR, and OoR SRAD funds Collaborating with, PIs, OoR senior editor(s), and methodologist in the conceptualization and design phases of grant proposals and other research projects Managing administrative facility requests, including, but not limited to Office of Research space allocation requests/usage and activities associated with research amplification Supporting Faculty Meeting with prospective faculty members to communicate college expectations related to all aspects of Anne’s College research enterprise, including expectations for faculty grant submission, programs aligned to successful proposal development and awards, and direct Office of Research (OoR) support in grant development, including faculty research agenda development, administration, and amplification Assisting faculty in applying for and obtaining external funding including, but not limited to, differentiating various support mechanisms managed by the OoR Evaluating faculty candidate readiness to engage in grant activities and high-impact research (e.g., proposal preparation skills, likelihood of obtaining funding to support research interests, working on grant projects, publishing in high-impact journals) Communicating with College leadership faculty candidate readiness to undertake a robust and impactful research agenda Collaborating with new faculty, in conjunction with appropriate OoR personnel, to discern research interest, develop research agenda, identify funding opportunities, and develop supportive plans to apply and obtain funding across various institution specific opportunities (e.g., FYAP program) Developing and implementing all programs and activities related to internal research catalyst funding Liaising with the Office of Research Development and Sponsored Research Administration to elevate and expand Anne’s College research footprint in campus-wide interdisciplinary research programs, including facilitating the management of internal grant applications, mock review panels, and faculty research profiles intra-institutionally Coordinating all research amplification activities, including targeted social media posts, facilitating the College’s Open Access Publishing program, and enhancing programs related to indexed journal article publishing Leadership Serving as a visible member of the Dean’s Cabinet Ensuring alignment of OoR activities with College strategic plans and policies Providing the Dean and the College leadership team with data analysis to support and inform research-related strategic planning and resource allocation decisions Chairing Strategic Planning Committee’s Academic Quality Subcommittee Administering the annual Dean’s Circle Catalyst Grant Program Leading the Academy of Scholars program and helping to coordinate all related activities throughout the year Ensuring the successful planning and implementation of College research events Coordinating all research partnerships with the Florida Department of Education Advising the College’s department chairs on the potential impact grant activities might have on faculty workload and SRAD distribution Working with the OoR Program Director and at the discretion of the Dean to provide administrative support and oversight to Florida State University Schools, FSU Pembroke Pines, and the Collegiate School at Panama City External Relations Attending, and serving as spokesperson at, College grant-related research meetings Establishing strategic professional relationships with key individuals within various funding agencies (e.g., IES, NSF, NIH, Spencer Foundation, W.T. Grant Foundation) Developing and maintaining effective collaborative relationships with all relevant individuals and groups (e.g., FSU VP for Research, other Associate Deans for Research, Director of the Office of Research Development, FSU Office of Research, LSI, FCRR) Serving as a member of the Council of Associate Deans for Research (CADR) Serving as the College’s representative member of the LEARN Coalition Representing the Dean or College/University interests at regional, national, or international conferences, convenings, or events at the discretion of the Dean Teaching Department responsibilities are limited to teaching and advising doctoral students Teaching responsibilities equivalent to one course per academic year in the fall or spring semester. Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in a discipline related to one of the academic units in the College. Demonstrated success in research that would warrant tenure in a discipline within the College Prior experience in academic leadership at the program, center, institute, department, or college level. Ability to analyze data and make data-informed decisions. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in navigating and establishing strategic professional relationships with key individuals within an institutional structure as well as governmental or private extramural funding agencies. Prior experience in developing and maintaining effective and collaborative college and campus relationships with individuals and groups relevant to the portfolio of responsibilities for the position. Prior experience developing programs to support faculty research and elevate institutional profile. Prior experience in supervision of organizational structures comparable to the Anne’s College Office of Research. Other Information The Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for an Associate Dean for Research position to start in July or August of 2027. For external candidates, the faculty rank associated with the tenure-track appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. The mission of the Office of Research (OoR) is to provide excellent service to the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences faculty in the development, administration, and amplification of research efforts. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Bob Eklund , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research leadership philosophy. Transcripts, work samples (such as journal articles or teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. This is a 9-month faculty position with a guaranteed summer appointment for the administrative role. Review of candidates will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63573&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "UGS Academic Advisor Pool - Fall 2026 (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "UGS Academic Advisor Pool - Fall 2026 (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63573 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Advising First – Division of Undergraduate Studies Responsibilities Responsible for advising undergraduate students in the development of academic schedules appropriate for stated education goals. Takes a proactive approach to academic advising, seeking out contact with students and staff, and providing advising services on request. Works with academic departments and other units within Undergraduate Studies to develop advising programs. Engages, helps plan, and participates in special projects for Advising First/UGST. Recommends changes and additions in existing policies and procedures that positively implement a successful advising program. Performs special projects as assigned by Undergraduate Studies. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of University rules and regulations. Prior customer service experience and /or experience working with students in an educational setting. Ability to extract complex academic information from various sources and maintain confidentiality. Experience and/or working knowledge of student advising, counseling, or working one-on-one with people in a professional or academic setting. Creative problem-solving skills. Master’s degree is preferred. Computer skills to include experience with Microsoft Office and web-based applications. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, goals, and objectives to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Ability to prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously with minimal to moderate supervision. Ability to deal with people in a calm, confident manner and with complete objectivity. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, parents, supervisors, and interdepartmental personnel. Attention to detail with a high standard of integrity. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $44,184, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
