    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63505&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS-Office Support (Full-Time)- FIN",
      "description": "OPS-Office Support (Full-Time)- FIN Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63505 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Through FIN , the FSU Learning Systems Institute collaborates with districts and schools to provide customized services and supports ensuring that all students with disabilities have the same educational, social, and future opportunities as their peers. FIN services and resources include (1) district capacity-building, (2) school-based planning, implementation, and support, (3) on-demand, web-based resources and products, and (4) family support and information. Responsibilities Serves as Office Support Specialist to FIN at Learning Systems Institute for students with disabilities (SWD) Staff: Provides coordination of travel activities for all team members to meet the needs of educational stakeholders across the State of Florida. Serves as one of the travel representatives for the team, processes and submits all travel requests, gathers documentation and submits travel reimbursement. Makes all necessary travel arrangements to include hotels, flights, car rentals as needed for faculty and staff in accordance with FSU policies and procedures. Ensures travel arrangements and reimbursements are processed in a timely manner. Responsible for assisting in the purchasing, shipping and distribution of supplies. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalency and two years experience; or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to four years. Preferred Qualifications Experience communicating effectively verbally and in writing. Experience establishing and maintaining effective working relationships. Experience gathering, interpreting, reporting, and/or editing information. Experience performing basic mathematical calculations. Experience prioritizing, organizing, and performing multiple work assignments simultaneously. Knowledge of applicable computer applications and basic computer functions. Contact Info FIN Network Email- lsi-finadmin@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range This position pays $19.00/hr. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63477&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (OPS) - Experimental, Modeling and Simulations of Magnetic Separations of Critical Materials (NHMFL)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar (OPS) - Experimental, Modeling and Simulations of Magnetic Separations of Critical Materials (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63477 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Responsibilities A postdoctoral position is available for highly motivated candidates to join a multi-disciplinary group of chemical engineers, physicists, chemists, and geochemists at the Florida State University (FSU) and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL). The project will involve experiments, modeling and simulations of critical metals fluids under influence of magnetic fields. The candidate selected is expected to conduct research on the experiments and modeling of a range of separation strategies for recovery of critical materials from industrial waste. The initial appointment will be for one year, with renewal for up to two additional years conditional upon performance and availability of funding. Qualifications PhD in Engineering and/or Physics or relevant discipline. Experience in computational fluid dynamics, magnet design and actuation, experimental micro/macro fluidics, colloidal science, and separation processes. Experience with instrument design and/or automation experience. Team player with leadership, communication, and presentation skills. A track record of quality publications with excellent writing skills is essential. Applicants should hold a PhD in chemical engineering, mechanical engineering, physics, or related fields, and have a strong background in chemical physics, experiments, flow visualizations, X-ray florescence, fluid dynamics, modeling, and simulations with COMSOL or other CFD platforms. Contact Info For information about this position, please contact Hadi Mohammadigoushki . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Please include: CV A statement of research interests The names and contact information of three references Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63504&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (College of Social Work)",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (College of Social Work) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63504 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Social Work Responsibilities The College of Social Work offers a collegial environment committed to maintaining a broad and supportive faculty community, supporting high quality and rigorous scholarship, and delivering high quality instruction. We invite applications for a 9-month, full-time, non-tenure track faculty position with opportunities for promotion and multi-year contracts. This position is fully on campus and in-person. Primary responsibilities include: Teaching and providing support to students in the BSW and MSW programs. Teaching a 4–4 course load (four courses in the Fall and four in the Spring), with opportunities to teach additional courses during the Summer term, depending on the need of the college. Engaging in college service and committee work as appropriate. Qualifications Master of Social Work from a CSWE-accredited program and two years of post-MSW clinical experience are required. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience and Clinical Social Work (LCSW) licensure or an equivalent credential. Additional preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate the ability to build strong community relationships and teach across the social work curriculum. Candidates with a doctoral degree are encouraged to apply Contact Info Lisa Jackson, PhD, LCSW Faculty Search Committee College of Social Work lisa.a.jackson@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit (a) cover letter describing interest in social work field education, related experiences, and teaching philosophy (b) current curriculum vitae; (c) evidence of teaching effectiveness (including copies of teaching evaluations with date); and (d) three names and contact information of people willing to provide letters of reference. Letters of reference will be requested from top applicants at a later date. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63459&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Beach Volleyball Head Coach (Part-time, OPS)",
      "description": "Beach Volleyball Head Coach (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63459 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University School Responsibilities Florida State University Schools (Florida High) is seeking a dedicated and student-centered Beach Volleyball Head Coach to lead and grow our middle school and high school beach volleyball program. The Beach Volleyball Head Coach will be responsible for fostering a positive, competitive, and developmentally appropriate environment that emphasizes sportsmanship, academic accountability, and athletic excellence. This position reports directly to the Athletic Director and is expected to uphold all FSUS, FHSAA, and FSU policies and procedures while supporting the mission and values of Florida High Athletics. Lead and supervise all aspects of the Beach Volleyball program (Middle School, JV, and Varsity Levels) Plan and conduct practices, conditioning sessions, and skill development activities Develop training plans that promote athlete safety, technical development, and competitive growth Schedule contests in accordance with guidelines and school policies Monitor and support student-athlete academic progress and eligibility Establish effective communication with student-athletes, parents, administration, and staff Coordinate game logistics, transportation, and supervision in alignment with FSUS policies Promote the program through school communication, social media, and community engagement Organize team events, awards, and end-of-season recognition Manage equipment, uniforms, field needs, and program inventory Ensure compliance with rules, district regulations, and FSUS clearance procedures Assist with off-season development, camps, clinics, and program growth initiatives Collaborate with youth and feeder programs to strengthen the long-term success of the beach volleyball program Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent Valid State of Florida Coaching Certificate (or ability to obtain) Current certifications in CPR, First Aid, Concussion in Sports, and Sudden Cardiac Arrest (required prior to season) Experience working with children and young adults in an educational or athletic setting Strong organizational, leadership, and communication skills Preferred Qualifications Previous beach volleyball coaching experience at the middle school, high school, club, or collegiate level Knowledge of rules and interscholastic athletics Playing experience at the high school, collegiate, or professional level College coursework or degree in Education, Kinesiology, Sports Management, or a related field Experience with player development, team management, and program building Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/Temporary job. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=59278&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I Adjunct - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I Adjunct - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 59278 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Nursing Responsibilities Applicants must be able to work in all clinical settings of the program. Provide instruction, service and support in accordance with college policies and procedures. Be able to lead a group of 8-12 nursing students in a hospital setting, focusing on teaching and facilitating learning in accordance with course outcomes. Facilitate teaching and learning of nursing skills such as critical thinking, clinical judgment, assessments, interventions, and evaluations. Qualifications Minimum degree requirements include completion of a Master's Degree in Nursing or related discipline. Must have an active, unencumbered, RN license in the state of Florida or Georgia (multi-state compact license preferred). University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63464&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Research Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63464 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University http://igc.fsu.edu Responsibilities The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University seeks candidates for up to five Research Faculty positions (at any rank) whose work addresses the topic of constitutional, economic, conscience, or educational liberty, broadly defined. We are particularly interested in candidates who will help us build what we are calling America's Liberty Lab. The Liberty Lab is a distinctive program that sets the IGC apart nationally. It uses the methods of the hard sciences and social sciences to study liberty itself. Just as traditional labs test hypotheses through experimentation and data, the Liberty Lab will investigate where and how liberty thrives-and where it does not. The Lab will serve as a hub for: data collection and empirical analysis across our four pillars of liberty (constitutional liberty, economic liberty, conscience liberty, and educational liberty); original survey research and public opinion polling; field and natural experiments on policy and institutional design; and evaluation of real-world laws and regulations. We are particularly interested in researchers whose work addresses real policy outcomes. We expect research faculty to publish in academic outlets as well as write white papers and other work read by policy makers. The goal is to link topflight academic research with nonpartisan public policy discussions. We see candidates from a broad array of academic backgrounds, including (but not limited to): political science, psychology, economics, communications, public policy, history, religion, and more. The successful candidate will be expected to show a commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Experience with cognitive experimental methods is not required but is a plus. Qualifications Completed Ph.D. by the date of hire. Research interests that contribute to the study of liberty and American civics. Potential for high impact publications. Commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the Institute for Governance and Civics. Contact Info Dr. Eric Olson, Economic Liberty Branch Head Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University eo26c@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. The position is being advertised as open rank and open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63466&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 9 Month Salaried - (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 9 Month Salaried - (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63466 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University https://igc.fsu.edu Responsibilities The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University seeks candidates for up to five Teaching Faculty positions (at any rank) to teach courses in our newly created Civics and Liberty Studies degree program. Our approach is what we are calling a renewed civic pragmatism. This interdisciplinary degree program consists of two parts. One part examines civic formation through the liberal arts. The other part focuses on social science. The program integrates classical and modern texts, empirical social science, legal analysis, and rhetorical training to develop thoughtful, data-informed, and ethically grounded civic leaders. We seek candidates from a broad array of academic backgrounds, including (but not limited to): political science, psychology, economics, communications, public policy, history, religion, philosophy, and more. The successful candidate will be expected to show a commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Qualifications Completed JD or Ph.D. by the date of hire. Research interests that contribute to the study of liberty and American civics. Potential for high impact publications. Commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Contact Info Dr. Phillip Pinell, Teaching Faculty Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University pp25n@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63467&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63467 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Dance Responsibilities The Florida State University School of Dance seeks a dynamic, collaborative leader to fill an Open Rank faculty position in Lighting and Visual Design while serving as Director of Production. This hybrid faculty-administrative position combines teaching, creative research, student mentorship, production design, and oversight of the School's production operations. The successful candidate will maintain an active program of creative and/or scholarly activity, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in lighting and visual design, mentor student artists and designers, and provide leadership for the planning, coordination, and execution of all School of Dance productions. Teaching and Student Mentorship Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in lighting design, visual design, projection design, stage technology, and related areas of expertise. Develop and teach elective courses aligned with the candidate's specialized knowledge and creative practice. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students in coursework, production assignments, portfolio development, and professional preparation. Serve on graduate thesis and dissertation committees and support student research and creative activity. Supervise and guide student lighting and visual designers through all phases of production. Creative Activity and Production Design Serve as the resident lighting designer for School of Dance productions. Design lighting and visual elements for departmental performances, concerts, and special events. Collaborate with faculty choreographers, guest artists, and production personnel to create cohesive artistic experiences. Integrate lighting, projection, digital media, and emerging technologies into performance environments as appropriate. Maintain an active record of creative and/or scholarly achievement consistent with tenure-track expectations. Director of Production Provide leadership for the planning and execution of the School's annual production season. Coordinate the production calendar, including rehearsals, technical rehearsals, performances, and special events. Work closely with the Production Manager, Production Assistant, faculty, staff, and guest artists to ensure effective production operations. Supervise technical production personnel, student employees, and production crews. Manage production-related budgets, equipment inventories, and resource allocation. Oversee the maintenance and safe operation of lighting, projection, and production equipment. Ensure compliance with university and industry safety standards and best practices. Service and Leadership Participate in School, College, and University governance through committee service and other assigned responsibilities. Contribute to recruitment, retention, and student success initiatives. Engage in professional service at the regional, national, and/or international levels. Support the School's mission through collaborative leadership and active participation in institutional initiatives. Qualifications Terminal degree (M.F.A. or equivalent) in Lighting Design, Theatrical Design, Dance Production, Theatre, Dance, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Minimum of five years of professional experience in lighting design, with significant experience designing for dance performance. Demonstrated expertise in lighting design processes, technologies, and production practices. Evidence of achievement in creative and/or scholarly work. Demonstrated commitment to teaching, mentoring, and collaborative artistic practice. Strong organizational, leadership, and project management skills. Preferred Qualifications Successful university-level teaching experience. Experience supervising production operations, technical staff, and production budgets. Experience with Qlab, Vectorworks software, LightWright, Eos systems, Dante software, and Paradigm. Expertise in one or more complementary areas such as: Projection or media design, Costume design, Scenic design, Filmmaking or digital media production, Musical composition or sound design, Dance technology, Related movement or dance practices Experience working across interdisciplinary artistic environments. Demonstrated commitment to excellence and student-centered learning. Other Information The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Dance has been included in Florida State University’s offerings for over 90 years, with a major degree program for more than sixty of those years. It has been recognized as a leader among college dance programs. Graduates of our programs include dancers, teachers, scholars, and leaders in companies, schools, universities, and art organizations in the United States and abroad. Montgomery Hall is one of the best dance facilities in the nation. The Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) is an internationally recognized dance research center and part of the School of Dance. This unique and visionary institute brings a steady stream of prominent and emerging dance artists to campus to create and develop the work that the rest of the world will experience in years to come. Add to this mix an esteemed faculty and talented students, and it is easy to see why we are excited for what is to come. Contact Info Associate Professor Daniel Smith , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are required to submit: Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three references. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to Ian Williams , Senior Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin on November 20th 2026, and will continue until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63436&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Educational Leadership and Policy, 9 Month Salaried - Educational Leadership and Policy Studies - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Educational Leadership and Policy, 9 Month Salaried - Educational Leadership and Policy Studies - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63436 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Engaging in a well-defined scholarship agenda with clear connections to K-12 educational policy and/or transitions to higher education. Teaching graduate courses in our online EdD program related to educational policy and/or research methods; Advising graduate students in the online EdD program and other programs as requested; Serving on student graduate committees, including chairing EdD student dissertations; Providing service to the university, the department, the college, and the profession; Developing and submitting grant proposals to funding agencies. Qualifications Earned doctorate in educational leadership, educational policy, or related education and/or social science disciplines; Evidence of high-quality scholarship (e.g., recent publications in peer-reviewed journals, working papers, recent presentations at national or international conferences); Commitment to and experience working with students of various backgrounds; Ability to teach educational leadership and policy courses and/or research methods courses; Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in qualitative research methods Experience with mentorship, in preparation for chairing EdD student dissertations; Experience with online teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Experience with teaching or training in research design courses (literature review, prospectus development, applied qualitative methods, etc.); Potential for success in garnering external funding for research. Other Information The Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies (ELPS) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant professor position. We seek a colleague committed to research, mentorship, teaching, and advising. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in ongoing research in well-defined scholarship areas with clear connections to K-12 educational policy, advise professional doctoral students in our online EdD program, chair EdD dissertation committees, contribute to academic service, and apply for external funding to support new research projects. ELPS strives to develop a deep understanding of, and respect for, our students and colleagues. The Department enrolls a sizable population of students in online EdD and master’s/specialist degree programs, in-person PhD and master’s programs, and hosts a program evaluation certificate program. We seek a colleague who is committed to and capable of effectively educating students across multiple programs, with a particular focus on advising EdD students. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/. For more information about the Department of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/elps . The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Search Committee Co-chairs: Erica Harbatkin and Eric Ludwig University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin October 9, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63441&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Clinical Exercise Physiology, 9 Month Salaried - Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, Human Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Clinical Exercise Physiology, 9 Month Salaried - Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63441 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Science in the Anne Spencer Daves College Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Develop and maintain a nationally and internationally recognized, extramurally funded research program in clinical exercise physiology, preventive medicine, chronic disease management/prevention, cardiometabolic health, rehabilitation, exercise interventions, healthy aging, metabolism, and related areas. Recruit, mentor, and guide graduate students through their academic and research endeavors, fostering their professional growth. Conduct high-impact research that reinforces and expands current departmental strengths in cardiometabolic health, skeletal muscle biology, gut microbiome, and immunity. Establish collaborative research partnerships with healthcare providers and investigators across FSU Health, affiliated clinical systems, and interdisciplinary teams to expand the scope and reach of the department’s research initiatives. Contribute to the department’s teaching efforts at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, designing and delivering courses aligned with your area of expertise. Develop innovative curricula and strategies to enhance student engagement and learning outcomes. Participate in departmental, college, and university service, including committee work, and engage in professional outreach activities. Engage in community and public outreach that promotes health, nutrition, and exercise science education (e.g., Exercise is Medicine). Qualifications Ph.D. in Exercise Physiology or a related field. Demonstrated success in teaching, research, and service commensurate with rank (Assistant or Associate Professor). Record of extramural funding to support research initiatives (Associate Professor) or evidence for the likelihood of obtaining extramural support (Assistant Professor). Strong scholarly productivity with peer-reviewed publications. Excellent communication skills and ability to work collaboratively within interdisciplinary teams. Appropriate Postdoctoral Training. ACSM Clinical Exercise Physiologist certification, or be willing to obtain this certification upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Priority will be given to those with established or emerging expertise and leadership in research related to clinical exercise physiology. Proven success with securing external research funding. Federally funded research program Experience with interdisciplinary research teams or collaborations. Evidence of effective teaching Other Information The Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences (HNFS) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant/associate professor position. We seek candidates whose research programs focus on the role of exercise in health, disease prevention, clinical care, rehabilitation, and/or healthy aging, and who can leverage emerging opportunities within FSU Health and its affiliated clinical partners. The ideal applicant is committed to research, mentorship, teaching, and academic service. The successful candidate will be expected to develop an extramurally funded research program that integrates exercise physiology within healthcare settings, contributes to improving patient outcomes, and supports graduate and postdoctoral trainees. For more information about HNFS, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/hnfs The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ Contact Info Michael J. Ormsbee, PhD University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of current/future research plans Statement of teaching interests Contact information of at least three professional references. Three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 10/15/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63440&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Clinical Nutrition, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Clinical Nutrition, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63440 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Science in the Anne Spencer Daves College Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Maintain a nationally recognized (and internationally recognized for Associate Professor applicants), extramurally funded research program in clinical and translational nutrition that advances the department's research mission. Conduct high-impact research that complements and expands departmental strengths in clinical and translational nutrition, metabolism, cardiovascular health, dietary nutrients and bioactive compounds, microbiome science, exercise and nutritional physiology, skeletal muscle biology, immunity, and healthy aging. Recruit, mentor, and supervise graduate students, postdoctoral scholars, and other research trainees. Develop collaborative research partnerships across FSU Health, Tallahassee Memorial HealthCare (TMH), and affiliated clinical and community-based organizations, including opportunities within the FSU Health Research and Collaboration Building. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas aligned with disciplinary expertise. Contribute to curriculum development and innovation to enhance student learning and workforce readiness. Participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities. Engage in community outreach and translational activities that promote nutrition, health, and disease prevention and/or management. Qualifications Ph.D. in Nutrition, Physiology, or a closely related field. Appropriate postdoctoral training or equivalent research experience. Demonstrated success in teaching, research, and service commensurate with rank. Evidence of the potential to obtain extramural funding (Assistant Professor) or a demonstrated record of extramural funding to support an independent research program (Associate Professor). Strong record of scholarly productivity, including peer-reviewed publications. Excellent communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively within interdisciplinary teams. Experience conducting human clinical research and/or experience working in healthcare or community-engaged research relevant to clinical and translational science. Preferred Qualifications Priority will be given to candidates with established or emerging expertise and leadership in clinical and translational nutrition research related to dietary patterns, phytochemicals and nutrients, precision nutrition, metabolism and metabolomics, nutritional physiology and pharmacology, cardiometabolic and gastrointestinal health, body composition, nutrition-related chronic disease, and/or eating and ingestive behavior. Evidence of a successful externally funded research program, with preference given to candidates with current or prior federal funding. Experience working within interdisciplinary research teams and collaborative research environments. Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) credential preferred. Evidence of effective teaching and mentoring. Experience in healthcare settings and/or community-engaged research relevant to clinical and translational science. Other Information Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Clinical Nutrition at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We seek scholars with strong research programs that complement the department's strengths in nutrition, metabolism, exercise physiology, food science, cardiovascular health, gut microbiome, skeletal muscle biology, immunity, and healthy aging. Candidates with expertise in clinical and translational nutrition are particularly encouraged to apply. Areas of interest include precision nutrition, dietary patterns, bioactive compounds and nutrients, nutrition-related chronic disease, metabolism and metabolomics, nutritional physiology and pharmacology, cardiometabolic and gastrointestinal health, body composition, and eating/ingestive behavior. We welcome scholars whose research integrates nutrition with human physiology, biomedical sciences, behavior, physical activity, and/or clinical and translational research, and who can contribute to the expanding FSU Health research enterprise. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with investigators and healthcare providers across FSU Health and affiliated clinical practices. The position offers access to state-of-the-art research facilities, interdisciplinary partnerships, and a dynamic academic environment committed to advancing nutrition, exercise physiology, food science, and health-related research. The Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences supports faculty success through opportunities for professional development, research growth, and leadership. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Sarah A. Johnson , PhD, RDN, FASN, Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit a letter of application, a statement of teaching interests, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Candidates selected for an interview will be required to provide transcripts and work samples (e.g., teaching materials or manuscripts). Letters of recommendation may be requested from finalists. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates are encouraged to apply as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63439&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I/II in Nutrition and Food Science, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I/II in Nutrition and Food Science, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63439 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Science in the Anne Spencer Daves College Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses within the Nutrition and Food Science program. Serving as the primary academic advisor and mentor for undergraduate and graduate students pursuing Food Science. Providing leadership and coordination for Food Science curriculum, assessment, and student success initiatives. Collaborating with faculty, staff, and students to strengthen and advance Food Science education within the Nutrition and Food Science program. Engaging in service that supports the department, college, university, community, and profession. Qualifications Doctorate in Food Science or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated experience teaching Food Science or related courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Relevant professional, industry, regulatory, extension, or applied experience in Food Science or a related field. Evidence of effective communication, collaboration, and student mentoring. Evidence of professional, university, and/or community service. Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating academic programs, advising students, or providing curriculum leadership. Demonstrated commitment to student success through advising, mentoring, and experiential learning opportunities. Other Information The Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month Specialized Teaching Faculty position. We seek a colleague with expertise in Food Science who is committed to excellence in teaching, student mentoring, academic advising, and program leadership. The successful candidate will serve as the primary teaching faculty member supporting Food Science education within the Nutrition and Food Science program. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Food Science and related areas of the curriculum, providing academic advising and mentoring to Food Science students, and contributing to the continued growth, coordination, and advancement of Food Science education within the department. The Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences at Florida State University is a dynamic academic unit serving approximately 1,000 undergraduate and 120 graduate students. The department offers undergraduate degree programs in Nutrition and Food Science, Dietetics, Exercise Physiology, and Athletic Training. Graduate programs include master's degrees in Nutrition and Food Science, Sports Nutrition, Exercise Physiology, and Sports Sciences, as well as doctoral degrees in Nutrition and Food Science and Exercise Physiology. The department also offers an accredited Dietetic Internship that prepares graduates for credentialing and professional practice as Registered Dietitian Nutritionists. Faculty in the department are engaged in nationally and internationally recognized research and scholarship spanning nutrition, food science, exercise physiology, and related health sciences. Areas of expertise include basic, applied, clinical, and translational research focused on nutrition, metabolism, cardiovascular health, physical activity, food systems, human performance, and healthy aging. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, student mentorship, and interdisciplinary collaboration to advance health and well-being across the lifespan. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu / Contact Info Jennifer Farrell , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin immediately and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
