    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63365&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Sport Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Sport Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63365 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to serve on doctoral committees and supervise student research, in addition to teaching and providing service to the program, department, college, and university. Candidates are also responsible for developing a program of research and scholarly activity in the realm of sport psychology. Qualifications Candidates for this position should have an earned doctorate from a recognized doctoral program in Sport Psychology or a closely related field (e.g., Kinesiology, Exercise Science). Preferred Qualifications Prior tenure-track experience and demonstrated potential or proven success in securing external research funding are highly desirable. Prior experience mentoring doctoral students is also preferred. Other Information The program is seeking a candidate with clearly expressed interest in sport psychology research and professional issues. The successful candidate will demonstrate an aptitude for conducting research, teaching, and mentoring graduate students, as well as a commitment to both the Sport Psychology MS and PhD programs. We are seeking a candidate who will contribute to strengthening program quality and student recruitment. The successful candidate will also demonstrate skills related to the quality teaching of sport psychology courses. This top-ranked program has a vibrant Sport Psychology Lab and connections to the Institute of Sport Science and Medicine (ISSM) . The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Search Committee Co-Chairs: Brady DeCouto David Eccles University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities – from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, a statement of teaching interests, and a research statement. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 10/02/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
