    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63386&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Violin, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Violin, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63386 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate-level violin students. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio. Serve on doctoral and master’s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include coaching chamber music and teaching courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Qualifications Hold a doctoral degree or demonstrate a record of equivalent performance and teaching experience. Hold a record of successful university-level studio teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Demonstrate a proven commitment to creating an environment which contributes to the vibrancy and economy of the university community and engages students. Other Information Seeking new knowledge and deeper understanding of music in interdisciplinary contexts through innovative research, music performance, and creative activity, The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and one of the largest university-based music programs in the nation. We are home to over 600 undergraduate and over 300 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 26 foreign countries. Contact Info Alexander Jimenez , Professor of Conducting and Director of Orchestral Activities University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In addition to the online application, please attach a single document that includes: Cover Letter (1-2 pages) Curriculum Vitae Contact information for four professional references (mailing address, phone, email). Links to video recordings made within the past five years that include: A 20-minute teaching video. A performance video (s) demonstrating a variety of styles. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin August 2027. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by September 28, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63374&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Elementary Mathematics Education School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Elementary Mathematics Education School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63374 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Applicants will be expected to engage in research and seek external funding related to Mathematics Education for Elementary Students, teach undergraduate courses (specifically elementary mathematics methods courses) and graduate courses, collaborate with Elementary Education faculty, advise and mentor Master’s and Doctoral students, conduct research that informs the field, collaborate with STEM faculty, and provide service to the university, local community partners, and the profession. Qualifications Earned doctorate in Elementary Education, Mathematics Education (or a related field such as Curriculum & Instruction with a focus on STEM education) by August 2027. A strong record of scholarship commensurate with position, as indicated by peer-reviewed journal publications, conference presentations, and collaborative projects. A productive and innovative research agenda that operates within a strong theoretical and empirical approach to understanding some facet of Elementary Mathematics Teaching or Learning Experience teaching at elementary and post-secondary levels. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience securing and/or working on externally funded research projects. Experience collaborating with STEM faculty and/or elementary schools. A research focus on learning technologies, AI, and/or data science in the context of mathematics and statistics teaching and learning. Other Information The School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant professor of Elementary Mathematics Education position to start in August of 2027. Faculty in the Mathematics Education Program in the School of Teacher Education strive to develop a deep understanding of, and respect for, our teaching candidates and colleagues. The fac ulty have a long history of internationally recognized scholarship and a track-record of award-winning scholarship and consistent external funding. Our goal is to inform the field’s understanding of mathematics teaching and learning through research and policy development aimed at transforming lives and striving towards collective wellness and more sustainable ways of being . For information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences, visit https://annescollege.fsu.edu . For more information about the program, visit https://annescollege.fsu.edu/mathematics-education The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Christine Andrews-Larson University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin Oct 2, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63400&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/FSU Libraries and Undergraduate Studies",
      "description": "Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/FSU Libraries and Undergraduate Studies Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63400 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional advancement operations professionals’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The position is responsible for developing, implementing, and managing an alumni engagement plan that supports the Division of University Advancement's goals, leverages the advancement infrastructure of the Student Success Collective (SSC), Undergraduate Studies and FSU Libraries and adheres to Council for Advancement and Support of Education (CASE) best practices and metrics. It leads college-wide initiatives that foster meaningful connections among students, alumni, donors, parents, friends and volunteers that contribute to philanthropic priorities. The role also oversees collection, maintenance, and strategic use of alumni data. Lead the development and execution of a comprehensive alumni engagement plan for FSU Libraries and Undergraduate Studies (UGS), through student and alumni enculturation programming, communications, activities and events. Foster participation in experiential learning, networking, philanthropy, and volunteerism by connecting current students with alumni through mentorship and engagement activities. Partner with FSU Libraries and UGS staff to enhance student-alumni interactions through in-person and virtual events. Plan and execute Unit-led events, including conference receptions, Homecoming activities, and outreach programs, ensuring seamless coordination and impactful experiences for alumni and key stakeholders. Align alumni engagement efforts with FSU Libraries and UGS fundraising priorities by integrating development goals into outreach programming that supports long-term donor relationships. Collaborate with FSU Libraries and UGS development and DUA donor relations teams to manage stewardship touchpoints that strengthen connections with donors and key stakeholders. Support and manage key FSU Libraries and UGS alumni volunteers, volunteer groups, or advisory boards/councils, partnering with the development team to foster meaningful involvement, engagement and leadership. This may include contributing to agenda development, conducting research and creating events that inspire and empower volunteer leaders. Recommend alumni for volunteer leadership roles and contribute to donor pipeline development through incorporating best practice for discovery, CRM documentation, and recommending potential donors to development colleagues. Leverage existing DUA programming (e.g., Alumni Affinity Networks, Seminole Clubs, Homecoming activities, Seminole 100 and Alumni Awards) to engage FSU Libraries and UGS alumni and ensure FSU Libraries and UGS colleagues are aware of programming. Support campus-wide alumni engagement by staffing signature and regional events, recruiting alumni volunteers, submitting alumni award nominations, and encouraging Seminole 100 applications. Curate and amplify compelling stories about FSU Libraries and UGS students, alumni and donors. Respond to alumni inquiries. Partners with FSU Libraries, UGS, and DUA communications teams to develop an alumni communications plan for that complements central DUA outreach to alumni and donors. Effectively convey key updates, news, and engagement opportunities from FSU Libraries, UGS, DUA, and FSU, ensuring meaningful connections to FSU Libraries and UGS alumni. May manage and distribute email campaigns for FSU Libraries and UGS alumni-facing communications. This may include generating content, creating graphics and collaborating with DUA, FSU Libraries, and UGS communications team members to develop email marketing strategy. Extracts data files to upload for email distribution lists. Evaluate alumni engagement communications; provide analytics and marketing reports on all aspects of email communications. Serve as the alumni data steward for the FSU Libraries and UGS, ensuring compliance with DUA data policies and procedures to maintain accuracy, security and usability, this includes identifying and coding student/alumni participation in key program areas. Analyze alumni demographics and engagement trends to develop targeted in-person and virtual outreach strategies, fostering deeper connections with key alumni segments. Establish and assess relevant metrics to evaluate engagement effectiveness, using data insights to refine strategies and optimize outreach. Recommend new initiatives and engagement opportunities based on alumni and donor feedback, leveraging insights to strengthen relationships and enhance involvement. Track expenses and process expense reconciliations adhering to FSU and DUA policies and procedures. May develop and manage an alumni engagement budget or other funds at the discretion of FSU Libraries or UGS. May supervisor one full-time staff position. Stay abreast of the changing landscape within higher education impacting alumni engagement. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63394&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/International Programs",
      "description": "Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/International Programs Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63394 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The position is responsible for developing, implementing, and managing an alumni engagement plan that supports the Division of University Advancement's goals, leverages the advancement infrastructure of the Student Success Collective (SSC), The Graduate School and International Programs, and adheres to Council for Advancement and Support of Education (CASE) best practices and metrics. It leads college-wide initiatives that foster meaningful connections among students, alumni, donors, parents, friends and volunteers that contribute to philanthropic priorities. The role also oversees collection, maintenance, and strategic use of alumni data. Lead the development and execution of a comprehensive alumni engagement plan for The Graduate School and International Programs, constituents through student and alumni enculturation programming, communications, activities and events. Foster participation in experiential learning, networking, philanthropy, and volunteerism by connecting current students with alumni through mentorship and engagement activities. Partner with Graduate School and International Programs staff to enhance student-alumni interactions through in-person and virtual events. Plan and execute Unit-led events, including conference receptions, Homecoming activities, and outreach programs, ensuring seamless coordination and impactful experiences for alumni and key stakeholders. Align alumni engagement efforts with Graduate School and International Programs fundraising priorities by integrating development goals into outreach programming that supports long-term donor relationships. Collaborate with Graduate School and International Programs development and DUA donor relations teams to manage stewardship touchpoints that strengthen connections with donors and key stakeholders. Support and manage key Graduate School and International Programs alumni volunteers, volunteer groups, or advisory boards/councils, partnering with the development team to foster meaningful involvement, engagement and leadership. This may include contributing to agenda development, conducting research and creating events that inspire and empower volunteer leaders. Recommend alumni for volunteer leadership roles and contribute to donor pipeline development through incorporating best practice for discovery, CRM documentation, and recommending potential donors to development colleagues. Leverage existing DUA programming (e.g., Alumni Affinity Networks, Seminole Clubs, Homecoming activities, Seminole 100 and Alumni Awards) to engage Graduate School and International Programs alumni and ensure Graduate School and International Programs colleagues are aware of programming. Support campus-wide alumni engagement by staffing signature and regional events, recruiting alumni volunteers, submitting alumni award nominations, and encouraging Seminole 100 applications. Curate and amplify compelling stories about Graduate School and International Programs students, alumni and donors. Respond to alumni inquiries. Partner with Graduate School, International Programs, and DUA communications teams to develop an alumni communications plan for that complements central DUA outreach to alumni and donors. Effectively convey key updates, news, and engagement opportunities from Graduate School, International Programs, DUA, and FSU, ensuring meaningful connections to Graduate School and International Programs alumni. May manage and distribute email campaigns for Graduate School and International Programs alumni-facing communications. This may include generating content, creating graphics and collaborating with DUA, Graduate School and International Programs communications team members to develop email marketing strategy. Extracts data files to upload for email distribution lists. Evaluate alumni engagement communications; provide analytics and marketing reports on all aspects of email communications. Serve as the alumni data steward for the Graduate School and International Programs, ensuring compliance with DUA data policies and procedures to maintain accuracy, security and usability, this includes identifying and coding student/alumni participation in key program areas. Analyze alumni demographics and engagement trends to develop targeted in-person and virtual outreach strategies, fostering deeper connections with key alumni segments. Establish and assess relevant metrics to evaluate engagement effectiveness, using data insights to refine strategies and optimize outreach. Recommend new initiatives and engagement opportunities based on alumni and donor feedback, leveraging insights to strengthen relationships and enhance involvement. Track expenses and process expense reconciliations adhering to FSU and DUA policies and procedures. May develop and manage an alumni engagement budget or other funds at the discretion of The Graduate School and International Programs. May supervisor one full-time staff position. Stay abreast of the changing landscape within higher education impacting alumni engagement. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) A valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63416&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of Post Award, Sponsored Research Administration",
      "description": "Director of Post Award, Sponsored Research Administration Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63416 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Sponsored Research Administration within the Office of Research seeks to fill the position of Director of Post Award. Responsibilities This position provides strategic leadership for and oversight of Sponsored Research Administration – Post Award and Cost & Data Management teams including but not limited to: supervision and training/cross-training for staff; post-award modifications; completion of sub-recipient risk monitoring, and invoice submission in alignment with sponsor and/or Uniform Grant Regulations; fiscal review of expenditures for reasonableness and accuracy, institutional commitments (fiscal), securing appropriate internal reviews and approvals; invoicing and collections; submission of interim and final financial reports; FSU response to all internal and external audits; cash management (LOC) drawdowns and reconciliation, indirect costs negotiations; preparation of reports on productivity of the research enterprise, and data quality assurance. This position facilitates and advance research and sponsored project activities through various efforts to include but not limited to promoting SRA as a customer-oriented department; increasing the collegiality between SRA and the campus community; and reviewing and analyzing policies, procedures, and practices with a goal of automating and streamlining and/or reducing administrative burdens to the extent possible. Participate in and lead efforts to deliver and continually improve research and sponsored project related training and educational opportunities for faculty, students and staff. This position keeps abreast of changing regulations to ensure fiscal compliance with sponsor and institutional policies, procedures, and regulatory guidance. Troubleshoot issues with federal, state, and local agencies which are problematic to the administration of sponsored projects. Develop and implement policies as needed for prudent management practices, compliance and accountability relative to sponsored projects administration such as 2 CFR 200, FAR and other state and sponsor regulations. Analyze, interpret and disseminate to the campus community information relative to federal, state, and sponsor regulations to ensure institutional compliance and consult with faculty, staff and administrators regarding compliance and other procedural issues. Provide expertise, guidance and leadership to academic and administrative senior management on compliance and sponsored research administration matters. Build strong relationships with campus administrators, faculty and staff; and work in partnership with other University offices to enhance the institution's research enterprise. Responsible for ensuring the development and operation of appropriate management information systems and databases that are adequate for the administration of post-award activities for the University's research and sponsored project activities including the implementation of new tools to automate office functions. Develop relationships with federal, state, and sponsor representatives and participate in professional development activities and organizations to keep abreast of changes and updates regarding sponsor requirements. Responsible for the formulation and administration of the annual operating budget for SRA Post Award and ensuring appropriate expenditure of all funds allocated. Performs other duties as assigned as it relates to post-award activities Qualifications Masters degree and five years of experience or a Bachelor’s degree and seven years of experience. Preferred Qualifications At least four years of experience in leadership of a post award department is preferred CRA, CPRA, CFRA, or comparable professional certification is preferred. Significant and progressively responsible leadership experience in sponsored research administration with a substantial emphasis on post-award administration. Experience within a large, complex research-intensive university environment, preferably a Carnegie R1 institution. Demonstrated expertise with federal regulations governing sponsored projects, including Uniform Guidance (2 CFR 200) and Federal Acquisition Regulations (FAR), as well as related sponsor requirements and state regulations. Experience leading audit responses, financial compliance programs, cost analysis activities, and institutional policy development. Proven success leading organizational change, process improvement initiatives, and technology-enabled operational enhancements. Experience supervising large teams and developing high-performing staff. Contact Info All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications should include, as separate documents, a CV or resume and a letter of interest addressing the themes in this profile. WittKieffer is assisting Florida State University in this search. Applications will be received until the position is filled. We strongly encourage candidates submit their materials as soon as possible for full consideration. Nominations and inquiries can be directed to: Jessica Herrington, Robert Springall, and Roxana Woudstra at FSUDirectorPA@wittkieffer.com . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63375&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - Elementary Education - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - Elementary Education - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63375 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the Elementary Education program, including but not limited to content specific methodology courses, Classroom Management, Curriculum Development, and Practitioner Research. Supervise pre-service teachers in K-6 educational settings, and/or various other content and general methods consistent with candidate expertise and program needs. Teach four courses in each of the fall and spring semesters and two courses in the summer. Provide service to K-12 schools, the Elementary Education Program, the College, and the profession. Qualifications Earned doctorate in Elementary Education, Curriculum & Instruction, or a related field. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. A minimum of three years teaching experience in K-12 educational settings. Commitment to and experience working with all student populations. Commitment to engaging with best practice initiatives in instruction and pedagogy, mentoring, and curriculum design and development. Preferred Qualifications Experience supervising pre-service teachers in K-6 educational settings Knowledge of and experience with current best practices in instructional strategies/methods in K-6 education consistent with the Elementary program curriculum and Florida education standards. Experience working with English Language Learners Experience mentoring pre-service and in-service teachers Successful teaching of face-to-face and online education courses at the college or university level. Other Information The School of Teacher Education is committed to high quality personnel preparation programs; service to the state of Florida; and high-quality scholarly research in elementary education, early childhood education, reading/language arts, foreign and second language education, special education, blindness and low vision, science education, math education, social science education, English education, and related areas. Programs consistently rank among the best in the nation, particularly the Curriculum & Instruction and Special Education programs. The School strives to provide undergraduate and graduate students with world-class training in teaching, research and professional development. Through the guidance and mentorship of faculty, students graduate to serve as educational leaders who will contribute to the betterment of a pluralistic, global society in the context of the state of Florida's needs for an educated, global-minded citizenry. In addition to mentoring and preparing the next generation of educators, faculty engage in a wide range of research activities. Faculty work routinely appears in prestigious publications and is cited by peers. Recent Academic Analytics National Rankings placed the School of Teacher Education as fifth in the nation for number of articles published and third in article citations. Furthermore, faculty receive support from a robust Office of Research to pursue research opportunities, professional awards, and more. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Laura Bell University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin October 19th and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62901&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Laser Safety Officer",
      "description": "Laser Safety Officer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62901 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Environmental Health and Safety Responsibilities Responsible for implementing and maintaining laser safety programs, which includes training staff, monitoring operations, and ensuring compliance with relevant safety standards and regulations. Responsible for complete knowledge of Federal and State regulations which relate to laser safety in a university environment. Develop and maintain laser safety programs and procedures in compliance with state and national regulations. Ensure all lasers and laser systems are registered and classified according to guidelines set by relevant authorities. Serves as the Certified Laser Safety Officer for the university community. Determines the exposure potential for non-ionizing radiation workers through laser hazard evaluations and protocols. Conducts regular inspections and audits of laser facilities and operations to identify potential hazards and ensure safety measures are in place. Investigate laser-related incidents or accidents, determining the cause and recommending corrective actions. Be well-versed in relevant safety standards and regulations set forth by organizations such as the American National Standards Institute (ANSI), Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA), and the International Electrotechnical Commission (IEC). Manage and monitor the disposal of laser decommissioning and update of laser inventory, in accordance with environmental regulations. Maintain records of laser safety inspections, incidents, training, and equipment maintenance. Ensures compliance with all regulations and ordinances. Performs periodic instrument calibration, adjusting and repairs when necessary. Performs inventory and leak testing of x-ray units in accordance with license conditions and all applicable regulations. Remain constantly vigilant to changes or advances that may have an impact on EH&S related programs through proactive methods such as audits, research, interactions with colleagues at related institutions and by attending professional courses or society meetings. Keep abreast of new developments in laser technology, safety standards, and regulations and incorporate this knowledge into the organization’s safety program. Immediately report any findings that may affect University programs to supervisors and assist in determining and implementing necessary policy changes to ensure best practices are realized. Member of the radiation safety committee and the laser safety subcommittee. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in physics, engineering, health physics, IH, or related scientific field and two years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years) Possess a Laser Safety Officer certification or the ability to obtain one within one year of employment. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63389&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Office of Accessibility Services (OAS) Testing Center Coordinator (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Office of Accessibility Services (OAS) Testing Center Coordinator (Multiple Positions) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63389 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Accessibility Services (OAS) Department of Student Support and Transitions (DSST) Florida State University 108 Student Services Building 874 Traditions Way, Tallahassee, Florida 32306-4167 Responsibilities Manages the daily operations of the testing center and supervises OPS proctoring staff. Prepares the facility, exam materials, and equipment for daily use. Ensures equipment is in proper working order. Promotes strong customer service, professionalism, confidentiality, and academic integrity. Guides students and instructors through test service eligibility, setup, and scheduling steps. Including additional support to students requiring special accommodation, such as individual proctoring needs coordination of DAW activities, OAS scholarship programming, and assisting in overseeing programs and services. Maintains the exam registration system and the exam calendar. Make scheduling adjustments and special provisions as able. Troubleshoots, resolves, and reports all issues that occur in the OAS Testing Center. Coordinates expanded Office of Accessibility Services (OAS) operations for final exam week in Fall and Spring semesters. This includes alternative schedules and extended hours. Assists with the development and implementation of internal and external, independent and collaborative programming (e.g., workshops, training, events, orientations, etc.). Including but not limited to: DAW and Graduation/Celebration (internal, OAS Students). Reviews exam policies and procedures to ensure compliance with all national and local proctoring standards. Researches assessment best practices and advises fellow staff accordingly. Completes special research projects to improve assessment services. Performs other duties as assigned that support academic integrity initiatives and the mission of the department. Qualifications Bachelor's and two years of experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years or experience. (Note: or a post high school education and experience equal to six years). Contact Info Amber Wagner or Elizabeth Rudisill Office: (850) 644-9566 Fax: (850) 645-1852 Email: oas@fsu.edu Office of Accessibility Services (OAS) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63381&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of Development, College of Social Sciences and Public Policy",
      "description": "Director of Development, College of Social Sciences and Public Policy Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63381 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Director of Development will strategically execute a personal solicitation program resulting in philanthropic support by maximizing the identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of prospects for gifts at the $100,000 and up level for College of Social Sciences and Public Policy. This individual will secure, on an annual basis, private support at the major and principal gift level and will be responsible for identification of potential major and principal gift prospects. The Director of Development will be expected to uphold and exemplify the operating practices of the Division of University Advancement while raising philanthropic dollars in support of the mission of Florida State University. Works with the Dean, and the other members of the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy development, communication and alumni team to develop and execute strategic fundraising initiatives on behalf of the College and the university. Develops, coordinates, and executes an annual major gift plan, implementing fund-raising activities designed to meet an established monetary goal while also hitting a set suite of metrics. Establishes new relationships resulting in philanthropic investment, maintains existing relationships, which may generate new philanthropic investments, and provides prospect/donor-related assessments and feedback for the College and the Division. Identifies, qualifies and sustains a donor prospect portfolio with individuals who have a giving capacity of $500,000 or more. Travels frequently, and secures gifts and pledges from alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of FSU. Exhibits and promotes a comprehensive understanding of the philanthropic priorities of the College, effectively matching the specific interests of prospects to those needs. Plans for and initiates direct activities with prospects that are designed to enhance the affiliation between the prospect and FSU. Effectively communicates FSU’s mission and represents FSU to external stakeholders. Central Development Collaboration Coordinates with the Division of University Advancement colleagues to identify prospects for planned giving, corporate and foundation giving in partnership with the Office of University Research, and principal giving in partnership with the Principal Gifts Team. Protects confidential information. Perform other related duties as required and assigned. Administrative/Events Assists in the facilitation of meetings, communications, informational exchanges and project / philanthropic coordination with the faculty and faculty chairs. Prepares proposals and gift agreements as required for proper gift documentation. Prepares correspondence with prospects and documents communications, solicitation activity and gift information in compliance with the FSU Foundation’s reporting guidelines. Creates, inspires, and maintains donor loyalty, interest and enthusiasm through stewardship communication and activities designed to express recognition, appreciation and the impact of their gift(s). Implementation of such a stewardship plan may include but should not be limited to letters, communication of unit or university initiatives, invitations to appropriate activities, meetings, events, student engagement or the facilitation of campus visits. Board/Volunteer Management Assists in the management of all volunteer boards associated with the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy. Qualifications Master's degree and four years of experience in a related advancement field or a Bachelor's degree and six years of related experience. Higher education can substitute for experience at a comparable rate. A valid Florida Driver's License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This role requires driving and travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63327&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63327 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College Of Criminology and Criminal Justice The College of Criminology and Criminal Justice at Florida State University is a vibrant academic community which fosters an environment of collaborative research and intellectual stimulation among its faculty and students. The College invites applications for assistant professor positions to begin Fall 2027. The areas of specialization are open. Responsibilities • Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a state university • Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities • Responsible for academic advising and related activities • May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees Qualifications Applicants must have demonstrated effectiveness in research and teaching. Candidates should have a Ph.D. in Criminology and Criminal Justice or a related field (such as sociology, psychology, or public policy). ABD candidates who anticipate degree completion no later than August 2027 will also be considered. A Juris Doctorate alone is not sufficient for consideration. Contact Info Any questions regarding the position may be directed to search committee chair Sonja Siennick at ssiennick@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Interested persons should complete an application and submit a cover letter, statements on research and teaching, and a curriculum vitae. In addition, they should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent to CCCJ-SearchCommittee@fsu.edu with the subject line “Letter of Recommendation for [applicant].” Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on September 28, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
