      "title": "Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Groundskeeper Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63847 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities Grounds and Landscaping Operations Responsibilities Performs grounds keeping tasks such as mowing, edging, raking, mulching, power blowing, weed eating, pulling weeds, light pruning, and watering plants. Responsible for debris removal, leaf removal, trash pickup and other tasks to keep grounds clean and presentable. Maintains areas by spreading landscape materials such as pine straw, bark, or rocks. Assists with landscaping tasks such as planting shrubs and trees. Assists in maintaining turf areas by utilizing push mowers to ensure an attractively landscaped environment on campus. Prepares landscaped areas with soil excavation, turf removal and re-sodding. Safely operates and maintains grounds equipment to ensure the health and appearance of university grounds. Ensures that all manual and power equipment is in proper working condition and reports maintenance problems to the supervisor. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor or higher authority. Qualifications Completion of a 9th grade education or higher. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Ability to work in inclement weather. Ability to use weedeater, backpack blower, and edger. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63837&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Cellular/Molecular Neuroscience)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Cellular/Molecular Neuroscience) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63837 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Biological Science | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Biological Science at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cellular/Molecular Neuroscience, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. Candidates with lines of laboratory research in any area of Neuroscience are encouraged to apply, particularly those using advanced in vitro and/or in vivo approaches to study neural circuits, synaptic structure, gene regulation, glial biology, neuroimmunology, neurodevelopment or disease mechanisms. Qualifications Candidates must have a doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization, postdoctoral training, and demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in research, teaching, mentoring and service, with clear potential or proven record for securing extramural funding to support an innovative research program. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to applicants whose research complements existing departmental strengths in epigenetics, systems neuroscience, sensory physiology, chemo-sensation, development, drug addiction, learning and memory, sleep and aging. Other Information This position offers the opportunity to join a dynamic, collegial, and supportive community within the Department and the broader, multidisciplinary Graduate Programs in Neuroscience, Molecular Biophysics, and Cell and Molecular Biology. FSU is classified as a Carnegie R1 (Highest Research Activities) University and ranks in the top 25 of National Public Universities (US News & World Reports). The Department of Biological Science is an interactive group with more than 40 tenure-track faculty members with expertise in neuroscience, sensory systems, developmental genetics, epigenetics, molecular biology, chromosome biology, evolution, ecology, conservation biology, genomics, structural biology, and virology. The Department is committed to the success of our faculty with engaged mentoring and significant resources. Researchers have access to excellent and fully staffed departmental and university research facilities that include an imaging facility with a Titan Krios electron microscope, confocal imaging, light sheet microscopy, BSL2 facilities, molecular cloning and hybridoma facilities, genomics, proteomics, metabolomics instrumentation, flow cytometry and mass spectrometry facilities, electronics and fabrication machine shop, and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory. Contact Info Inquiries about the position should be directed to Roberto Vincis , Search Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants will need to submit: 1) a cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) a research statement (max 3 pages), 4) a teaching statement (max 2 pages), 5) a list (with online access links) highlighting up to four peer-reviewed papers, 6) the names and contact information for up to 3-4 individuals who would be willing to provide a letter of recommendation. Letter writers will only be contacted for short-listed applicants. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on December 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63849&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Business Manager - UBA / Human Resources",
      "description": "Business Manager - UBA / Human Resources Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63849 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators - Human Resources Responsibilities About This Role The Office of Human Resources is seeking a Business Manager to oversee the financial and administrative operations that support Human Resources and the Employee Assistance Program. This position serves as a key partner to department leadership, ensuring effective fiscal management, operational excellence, compliance, and business continuity across a broad range of functions. Why This Role Matters As Business Manager, you'll provide financial and operational leadership helping Human Resources effectively support employees across Florida State University. Your important work will drive informed decision-making, sound stewardship of resources, and operational excellence across one of the university's most essential functions. What You'll Do Financial Strategy & Budget Management Serve as Budget Manager for Human Resources and the Employee Assistance Program. Lead budget planning, forecasting, reconciliation, and financial reporting activities. Monitor financial transactions and ensure compliance with university policies and procedures. Develop and maintain internal controls that support sound fiscal stewardship. Business Operations Oversee accounts receivable processes associated with the Background Check auxiliary program. Manage vendor payments, financial transactions, and issue resolution. Develop, document, and improve business processes and operational procedures. Support strategic initiatives and special projects that contribute to departmental goals. Human Resources Administration Serve as the departmental approver for job postings, job offers, and ePAFs. Monitor payroll and staffing allocation reports while assisting with issue resolution. Support compliance and operational effectiveness across HR functions. Leadership & Partnership Provide leadership and guidance to staff supporting fiscal and administrative operations. Build collaborative relationships across the university. Partner with stakeholders to achieve department objectives and support university initiatives. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Ability to independently manage business and fiscal operations in a complex environment. Experience developing solutions, improving processes, and driving operational efficiency. Strong financial management, analytical, and organizational skills. Demonstrated ability to build partnerships and serve as a trusted advisor to leadership and stakeholders. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
