    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63359&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Health Promotionists/Behavioral Health Coaches (OPS), Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine - College of Medicine",
      "description": "Health Promotionists/Behavioral Health Coaches (OPS), Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine - College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63359 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine The Spring Lab in the Department of Behavioral Science and Social Medicine is seeking a highly motivated, experienced Health Promotionist/Behavioral Health Coach to provide behavioral counseling and health coaching to participants in an NIH-funded randomized clinical trial through the SMARTer Weight Loss Management Study at Florida State University College of Medicine Join a dynamic interdisciplinary team conducting research on behavioral risk factors for chronic diseases (such as poor-quality diet, physical inactivity, obesity, and tobacco use). The lab develops, optimizes, and evaluates cutting-edge, technology-supported interventions to improve self-regulation, engage social support, and facilitate healthful behavior change. Responsibilities Provide individualized behavioral counseling and health coaching to study participants using evidence-based behavioral weight management strategies. Utilize Motivational Interviewing (MI) and other evidence-based counseling techniques to support behavior change and healthy lifestyle goals. Establish collaborative relationships with participants and tailor coaching strategies to individual needs, barriers, and readiness for change. Deliver intervention sessions in accordance with the study protocol and intervention manual. Document participant contacts, intervention delivery, and relevant participant information accurately and promptly. Participate in training, supervision, team meetings, and ongoing treatment fidelity assessments. Collaborate with research staff and investigators to support participant recruitment, engagement, retention, and study operations. Contribute to research reports, presentations, abstracts, manuscripts, and other dissemination activities. Contribute to qualitative data collection and analysis, including coding, thematic analysis, and identification of patterns across participant experiences. Assist with development and maintenance of qualitative codebooks and coding procedures. Qualifications Degree in counseling, psychology, social work, public health, health promotion, behavioral science, clinical research, or a closely related field. The successful candidate must demonstrate excellent organizational, verbal, written, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently, strong attention to detail, and a proven track record of excellence. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree. Experience providing behavioral counseling, health coaching, Motivational Interviewing, or a related behavioral intervention. Experience working with individuals on behavior change, lifestyle modification, weight management, chronic disease prevention/management, or related health behaviors. Ability to work collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research team. Experience working with human subjects research, ideally clinical trials. Experience delivering behavioral weight management or lifestyle interventions. Experience with REDCap. Experience with treatment fidelity assessment or behavioral intervention research. Experience preparing research abstracts, manuscripts, or presentations. Experience with qualitative research and data analysis, including coding and thematic analysis. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Full-time hours. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63808&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Faculty, 12 Month Salaried (Multiple Vacancies), Center for Advanced Power Systems",
      "description": "Research Faculty, 12 Month Salaried (Multiple Vacancies), Center for Advanced Power Systems Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63808 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) Responsibilities Multiple Research Faculty positions are available in cybersecurity, cyber-physical systems security, control and estimation of cyber-physical systems, with specific application to energy delivery systems and autonomous systems. Successful candidates will join a team of researchers at the Center for Advanced Power Systems at Florida State University and work closely with industry collaborators to develop and deliver systems and methods to protect critical infrastructures using cutting-edge Zero-Trust Architectures (ZTA), controls, ML/AI, and optimization. While a strong theoretical background is desired, the position is mainly application-driven with actual product delivery expected to industry partners. Qualifications Appli cants must have earned a doctoral degree from an accredited institution in releva nt field or a closely related field and demonstrate strong potential for outstanding research and leadership. Applicants with strong mathematical background in control theory, ML/AI, convex optimization, and hands-on experience with one or more of the following application areas (other closely related areas) are encouraged to apply: (1) Power systems modeling and simulation (2) AI/ML and cybersecurity, (3) cyber-physical security (3) multi-agent systems (4) Real-time simulation, HIL, CHIL and PHIL. Strong leadership qualities. Some experience in writing research proposals and reports. Strong foundation in mathematical analysis, physics-based models, optimization techniques, and AI/ML. Deep understanding of controls and systems dynamics (power systems/power electronics modeling) Research experience with strong publication record (or potential) and good presentation skills. Hands-on experience with real-time simulation and hardware implementation. Proficient programming skills (e.g., MATLAB/SIMULINK and Python). Due to federal contractual requirements, candidates must be a US Citizen or a US Permanent Resident. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated capabilities (through hands-on experience and/or strong publications) in relevant areas is preferred. Experience with OPAL-RT and/or RTDS is a big plus. Contact Info Rachel Brouwer , 850-645-2157 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This job opening serves to recruit for multiple specialized Research Faculty positions. The level of the positions will be commensurate with candidate qualifications. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63853&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "ASCENT Administrative Specialist (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "ASCENT Administrative Specialist (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63853 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Sponsored Programs ASCENT | FSU Panama City Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay, and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Assists in the management and administration of specialized program functions. Develops and instructs specific technical training for students and teachers as needed. Serves as the primary contact for specified programs supporting ASCENT, traveling as needed to visit partner schools, community groups, and local agencies. Works with local schools and community partners to align initiatives and create opportunities for students to be connected with technical education/certification opportunities. Works with testing center to assist with exam-scheduling and proctor services for instructors and students. Prepares impact & annual reports and researches select exam sessions & software features to aid in departmental support of student achievement. Occasional regional travel (Escambia, Santa Rosa, Okaloosa, Walton, Bay, Gulf, Franklin, and Wakulla County) and may require occasional evening and weekend work for events and special programs. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications K-12 Experience. Technical Training. Excellent communication skills. Contact Info Brianne Biddle University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $42,998, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position will begin in Winter 2026. This position will involve occasional regional travel (Escambia, Santa Rosa, Okaloosa, Walton, Bay, Gulf, Franklin, and Wakulla County) and may require occasional evening and weekend work for events and special programs. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63833&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist (Psychology)",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist (Psychology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63833 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | Florida State University College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The administrative specialist is responsible for coordination and oversight of daily front office operations, including handling initial client service requests, facilitating check-in for client appointments, recruiting, hiring, training, and supervising part-time office assistants. The administrative specialist is responsible for day to day activities related to the Psychology Clinic and Anxiety and Behavioral Health Clinic operating funds, including assisting in developing, monitoring, and adhering to annual operating budgets. Client billing, procurement, and monthly ledger reconciliations are required. The administrative specialist also monitors, coordinates renewals for, and maintains security of clinic inventory including for equipment, facilities, and specialized clinical materials. Adherence to HIPAA and FERPA is required. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience working with budgets, financial data, and Microsoft Excel, including the ability to organize, analyze, and maintain financial information is preferred. The ability to prepare and monitor a budget is required as is knowledge of computer applications and functions. The administrative specialist must be able to deal with crises, manage sensitive information, and adhere to ethical business practices and behavior. Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated starting salary for the position is in the mid-$40,000s. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
