      "title": "Facilities Superintendent (Psychology)",
      "description": "Facilities Superintendent (Psychology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63844 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | Florida State University College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities Oversee building operations, maintenance, and renovations across departmental facilities, coordinating with university service units and outside contractors to resolve issues and maintain functional research, instructional, and administrative spaces. Regular movement between departmental facilities is required. Coordinate equipment installation, maintenance, relocation, and removal, including management of departmental equipment inventories, annual inventory processes, and property transfers. Manage the departmental vehicle fleet, including scheduling, maintenance, and repairs. Serve as the departmental liaison for custodial services, Environmental Health and Safety (EH&S), workers’ compensation, emergency preparedness, and facility security. Manage building, laboratory, classroom, and clinic access, including electronic swipe cards and physical keys. Oversee departmental records retention and disposition, ensuring the secure storage and appropriate disposal of records, client files, and research data. Coordinate laboratory and office space planning, new laboratory setup, renovations, and facilities projects, including preparing cost estimates and coordinating approved modifications. Manage laboratory decommissioning when faculty depart, including equipment redistribution, property transfers, hazardous material disposal, surplus property processing, and laboratory cleanup. Serve as departmental Property Custodian and coordinate with university offices, faculty, and staff on equipment management, facilities' needs, and compliance requirements. Hire, train, and supervise OPS and Federal Work-Study employees. Serve as an after-hours emergency contact for designated facilities and as Critical Personnel during university closures. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and four years of experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to four years. Preferred Qualifications Strong organizational, communication, problem-solving, and project coordination skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, maintain accurate records, and work independently. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, university personnel, and outside contractors. Experience with facilities management, building maintenance, or equipment and property management. Experience in a research or laboratory environment. Knowledge of workplace safety, environmental health and safety, and emergency procedures. Experience supervising employees. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in