    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63807&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Researcher, OPS (Translational Behavioral Research - College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Researcher, OPS (Translational Behavioral Research - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63807 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Translational Behavioral Research - College of Medicine Responsibilities Supports the implementation of behavioral health research and intervention activities through participant engagement, study coordination, and program operations. Delivers study interventions, supports participant recruitment and retention, maintains study documentation, and collaborates with research and program teams to ensure high-quality, compliant study execution. Contributes to outreach, educational initiatives, community partnerships, and special projects that advance the goals of the SIU-FL program and associated research initiatives. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications Associate or bachelor’s degree in public health, health sciences, psychology, social work, behavioral science, or a related field. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Good organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines. Ability to build positive relationships with participants, team members, and community partners. Basic computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office applications. Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow study protocols, standard operating procedures (SOPs), and policies. Willingness to learn new research procedures, intervention techniques, data collection systems, and telehealth platforms. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively to a collaborative team. Commitment to working respectfully with a variety of individuals and providing responsive support. Previous experience in research, healthcare, public health, health education, customer service, or community outreach. Familiarity with participant recruitment, scheduling, data entry, recordkeeping, or administrative support. Interest in behavioral health, lifestyle counseling, or evidence-based intervention approaches. Experience working with adolescents, young adults, or a variety of communities. Interest in HIV prevention and treatment, sexual health, health education, or health disparities. Experience participating in community events, educational activities, or outreach initiatives. Familiarity with virtual meeting platforms and remote communication tools. Motivational Interviewing (MI) training or experience is a plus but is not required. Passion for working with health disparities. Contact Info Jonathan Morgan Program Coordinator University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is a full-time OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
