      "title": "Graduate Student Success Analyst",
      "description": "Graduate Student Success Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63852 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Institutional Research at FSU Responsibilities This position is responsible for developing analyses and reports to assist with the measurement of student success metrics and evaluation of student success initiatives. Responsibilities include: Responsible for executing analyses related to accreditation, admissions, enrollment, retention, student finances, graduation, and/or post-graduation outcomes of graduate students at FSU. Supports the Graduate School, colleges, departments, and other university units in applying student success analytics to local decision-making and program improvement efforts. Supports the development and stewardship of datasets used for graduate student success analytics. Develops and maintains data visualizations and dashboards that support graduate student success decision-making. Provides decision-support services to university stakeholders by integrating knowledge gained through analytical, dataset development, and data communication activities. Conducts trainings and workshops to promote data literacy across campus that directly or indirectly support graduate student success analytics. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a related field and two years of experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: or a post higher education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Master's degree preferred Preference for advanced degree in statistics, economics, or research sciences with high statistical engagement Proficiency in data analysis, visualization, and software tools such as Power BI. Ability to establish effective working relationships with stakeholders. Familiarity with SQL is preferred but not required. willingness to learn is essential Proven executive communication skills with the ability to discuss complex data and insights confidently with senior leaders Other Information Our Mission: Our mission is to deliver strategically relevant data and analyses that support student success, faculty excellence, and operational efficiency. We drive decision-making through compliance reporting, analytics, and data governance, supported by training and consultation services that cultivate a culture of informed leadership and continuous improvement. Our Vision: Our vision is to be at the forefront of decision intelligence by leading a collaborative, data-engaged culture and having a meaningful impact within the university, our state, and the field of institutional research. What We Do: Strengthen Data-Informed Student Success Advance Institutional Excellence and Accountability Optimize Transparency and Accessibility of Analytics Foster Collaboration and a Data-Engaged environment Helpful Who We're Looking For: The ideal candidate is a detail-oriented problem-solver with strong analytical skills who thrives in dynamic environments. You are comfortable managing multiple projects, presenting complex data insights, and collaborating across various teams. You are eager to learn, adapt, and make a measurable impact on the university's success. What to Expect: In the first 60-90 days, you will get up to speed with FSU's student success efforts, familiarize yourself with key systems and stakeholders, and begin contributing to high-priority projects. Training and mentoring will support your integration into the team, with opportunities to engage in hands-on analytics work. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary range to begin in the $50,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This posting is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63589&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Instructional Technologist - Herbert Wertheim College of Business",
      "description": "Instructional Technologist - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63589 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Academic Technology - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Academic Technology Support & Problem Solving Supports faculty and staff in the implementation, use, troubleshooting, and optimization of Canvas and an ecosystem of integrated academic technologies (e.g., Design PLUS, Kaltura, Simple Syllabus, Ally Course Report, and related tools) used to deliver undergraduate and graduate courses in online, hybrid, and on-campus modalities. Researches knowledge bases and/or credible resources, collects information from multiple different resources, evaluates information, identify solutions, and collaborates with internal and external stakeholders to resolve academic technology problems. Troubleshoots learning management systems, lecture capture systems, and an ecosystem of integrated academic technologies (e.g., Design PLUS, Kaltura, Simple Syllabus, Ally Course Report, and related tools). Provides guidance and consultation to faculty regarding the selection, implementation, and effective use of academic technologies to support teaching and learning needs. Course Lifecycle Management Supports course preparation, content migration, section management, course readiness activities, content maintenance, and continuous improvement efforts across undergraduate and graduate courses in online, hybrid, and on-campus modalities. Assessment & Assessment Technology Support Supports faculty in the creation, implementation, configuration, troubleshooting, and effective use of assessment technologies and workflows, including Canvas quizzes, gradebooks, accommodations, testing center processes, proctoring solutions, and related tools and methods. Collaboration & Continuous Improvement Collaborates with Academic Technology team members, Information Technology, Office of Digital Learning and Academic Technology, vendors, and other stakeholders to support academic technology workflows, maintain awareness of emerging learning technologies, best practices, and institutional processes. Participates in professional development activities and evaluates emerging learning technologies, processes, and practices to support continuous improvement and innovation within the Academic Technology unit. Shares relevant updates, resources, and recommendations with team members to promote effective adoption and use of academic technologies. Other responsibilities as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Contact Info Ömer Arslan Director of Academic Technology University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
